-Bind, Gravity Intensification, Internet Acuity, Matter Control, Occult Singularity, Opener of Ways, Plant Control, Refuge, Shadow Command, Traumavore, Vocalization<br /> <br /> <b>Cephalist:</b> Clairvoyance, Emotion Amplification<br /> <br /> <b>Chimeric:</b> Beast Mastery, Body Modification<br /> <br /> <b>Coactive:</b> Emulate, Soul Seer<br /> <br /> <b>Invasive:</b> Matter Emulation, Mechanical Transformation<br /> <br /> <b>Mutant:</b> Cursed Flesh, Gestalt<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Scars</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Controlled:</b> Aftermath, Scapegoat, Shame<br /> <br /> <b>Involuntary:</b> Asset, Obligation<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> Animal Enmity, Cyclical Scar, Evil Twin, Hubris, Lumbering, Masochism, Nameless, Noblesse Oblige, Omega, Overconfident, Reckless, Sleepy, Traumatic Memories, Undesirable, Weak Point<br /> <br /> <b>Standard Deviations:</b> Blight, Capacitor, Caveat, Cyclical Variation, Dependent Variation, Exclusive, Intimate, Naked Variation, Tethered, Twined Scars, Unreliable, Vampiric</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me so happy to see. So many of these are either one's I've homebrewed or wanted to so I can't wait to see how they are gonna be done officially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T04:02:17-07:00","id":1536049,"title":"","content":"It's Tuesday and time for more previews of <b>Shallow Graves</b>. As with last week, I've posted one excerpt here, but a second is available for free at the Patreon in my signature (as is the full text of the first half of the chapter, for paid members).<br /> <br /> Chapter One explores the personal impacts of the Divergence to make it easier to get inside the heads of the Broken when roleplaying. Its first half unpacks Origin, Clades, souls, lost Anchors and Aspirations, and Acclimation. Its second half focuses on Touchstones, including more details about what constitutes &quot;furthering a Touchstone&quot;, roleplaying guidance and systems for Faltering and reversals (i.e., changing a Conviction Touchstone to a Loyalty Touchstone or vice versa), and some ideas advice for choosing Touchstones (including several examples of some unusual Touchstones of each type). On with the preview!<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Origins</span></b><br /> <br /> Origins reflect a character\u2019s state of consent at the moment of Divergence. While some Remade retain the same attitude towards their transformation now that they had then, many have evolving views of the net cost/benefit of their Divergence. If they had it to do again, some Exomorphs would have welcomed the power they gained when they were Broken, and no few Autourgics discover they regret their transformations. Origin should therefore be considered a starting point, not a reflection of a character\u2019s current attitudes towards their Remade condition. Any Origin can lead a Deviant to life as a Renegade (or a Devoted).<br /> <br /> A character\u2019s Origin often says more about the conspiracy that made them than it does about the Deviant themself. Moreover, a conspiracy\u2019s preference of Origin can evolve over time.<br /> <br /> Below are 50 Deviant backstories that lead Remade to become Renegades. They\u2019re organized by Origin, but most could just as easily apply to a character of another Origin. For example, the Exomorph might well have grown sympathetic towards the conspiracy that made her, only to run afoul of a bad boss or workplace rival who drove her to go rogue. Remember also that while all paths in these character concepts lead to Renegades, the roads to becoming Devoted are just as numerous and varied.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Autourgic Renegades</span></b><br /> <br /> Conspiracies with a large population of Elect are often among the most ethical in the Web of Pain. This is certainly relative. These conspiracies must still violate their subjects\u2019 bodies and minds in unthinkably awful ways to trigger the Divergence. But at least those they recruit go into the process with the risks clearly disclosed, even if they can\u2019t truly understand what the experience will be like. Autourgic-heavy conspiracies rely on their recruits\u2019 loyalty and dedication to a cause or ideal. Many are government-sanctioned groups that can wave the flag of nationalism to win over patriots, while others are religious orders that can rely upon their adherents\u2019 zeal to ensure a steady supply of willing subjects. Elect-heavy conspiracies are also the most likely to know about and fight against hostile supernatural forces in the world, sharing this knowledge with potential Divergence candidates to inspire them to offer themselves as soldiers in that hidden war. A large minority of conspiracies begin with a Self-Made Autourgic as a founder.<br /> <br /> In times when the body count rises, or cultural factors make patriotism, zeal, and sacrifices for the greater good a less common refrain in the population, Autourgic-dominated conspiracies must often adapt. Many turn to recruiting existing Remade, either poaching them from rival conspiracies or seeking out Renegades or Pathologicals who might be stirred by the conspiracy\u2019s higher purpose. Sufficiently desperate conspiracies, finding it impossible to meet their recruitment goals in any other way, might resort to deception or outright abduction to meet their quotas (producing Epimorphs and Exomorphs).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a successful conspiracy with a large pool of Autourgic Devoted may unlock the secrets of producing Genotypals, laying the foundation for an important shift in its focus. This is by no means assured, however, since it depends on whether the conspiracy is able to isolate the root cause of one type of Divergence and reliably reproduce it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bad Apple:</b> Divergence offered you power, which you have long craved. You didn\u2019t much care what the conspiracy\u2019s true goals were as long as you benefited. For a long time, you did. You did your job, but you also enjoyed the power your Variations granted you outside of working hours. Technically, you signed a code of ethics or behavior or some shit, but adhering to it never crossed your mind. You were one of the conspiracy\u2019s few success stories. You were irreplaceable, far too precious to discard over some venial violation, whether it was exacting petty revenge on old enemies or earning a few grand extra selling your unique services to outside parties. Then those bastards told you they weren\u2019t going to let you work for them anymore. You were giving their whole organization a bad name, and finance ran some numbers with the PR department and decided you were costing them more money than you were earning. They\u2026fired you. Like some incompetent custodian or a telemarketer who missed her quota one month too many. But you\u2019ll show them they\u2019ve made a grave mistake.<br /> <br /> <b>Corruption:</b> The conspiracy used to be something you could believe in \u2014 not perfect, but basically well-intentioned and filled with people who wanted to make the world a better place. You\u2019re not sure exactly when that changed. Maybe it was the new CEO. Maybe it was the IPO. Maybe it was after the head of R&amp;D was killed in that laboratory accident. Regardless, it isn\u2019t the same place anymore. It isn\u2019t a good place to work, and any good it might still be accomplishing is far outstripped by the harm it inflicts. So, you left. It wasn\u2019t easy. You still have friends there, after all. But you know it was the right decision.<br /> <br /> <b>Discarded:</b> You chose Divergence, chose it knowing something of what it would cost you, knowing there could be no turning back. You woke with remarkable gifts. You woke with a confidence you had never felt in your life. Then you saw the frowns on the faces of the scientists as they tested you. You had gained impossible powers, but maybe they weren\u2019t as potent or as useful as the conspiracy had hoped. Or perhaps the burdens you gained during the process were too disruptive or more severe than was acceptable. It\u2019s even possible that your new abilities were <i>too</i> powerful, and the conspiracy feared it wouldn\u2019t be able to control you. Whatever the case, they decided they didn\u2019t want you. They might have flown you to an unfamiliar, faraway city and abandoned you, or perhaps you woke up one day and found that they had taken all their equipment and staff and left for places unknown. Either way, you don\u2019t know how to find them, and doubt they would take you back even if you did.<br /> <br /> <b>Extinct Conspiracy:</b> The conspiracy was home to you when you had nowhere else to go and no one else to care for you. You liked working there. You liked your coworkers. You believed in its mission. Yours was the first name on the list when they asked for volunteers for a special new treatment. But then something happened. At the time, you thought it a catastrophic accident, one that in an instant took away everyone and everything you loved. You only survived because of your remarkable abilities. As you picked through the rubble, looking for survivors, you discovered evidence of foul play. Now you seek the ones responsible.<br /> <br /> <b>Mission Accomplished:</b> You volunteered for the Divergence out of a sense of duty or to achieve an objective that would have been impossible without the power it granted. It was an act of self-sacrifice you embraced at the time and didn\u2019t regret afterwards. Whatever it is that drove you to choose Divergence, you accomplished it. That was supposed to be the end. You turned in your resignation \u2014 or your Progenitor released you from his service as agreed when you volunteered \u2014 and you walked away. But then you started to notice the black sedans waiting wherever you went. One day, a gentleman in a well-tailored suit got out of one and made you an offer: use your powers in the service of his employer. You refused him, but he and his associates have proven unwilling to take no for an answer.<br /> <br /> <b>New Boss:</b> You were satisfied with your life at the conspiracy until <i>he</i> arrived. Maybe he was part of a routine management shake-up, or maybe he forced out (or murdered) your previous boss. Maybe he still claims to be the same boss as ever, but he acts like a different person. The point is that he was trying to make your life miserable (or planned to get rid of you in a permanent fashion), so you took action. You may or may not have gone berserk at your office and left his body in a shallow grave before you left, but you\u2019re out now, and there\u2019s no going back.<br /> <br /> <b>Self-Loathing:</b> You volunteered for the process or ritual that led to your Divergence, but you realized almost immediately that it was a mistake. You hate what you\u2019ve become, and you hate the ones who convinced you to go through with it even more.<br /> <br /> <b>Truth Revealed:</b> The conspiracy seemed benevolent, at first. You served it loyally, gave more of yourself to it than was probably wise. But gradually you became aware of some questionable practices. You brought them to your superior\u2019s attention, and she assured you that these violations would be investigated, the perpetrators disciplined. Except that didn\u2019t happen, so you started looking into matters on your own, which led you to a terrible truth. These awful practices weren\u2019t anomalies; they were standard procedure. The more you looked, the more you realized your beloved organization was a cancer in the world. Most of those it Remade didn\u2019t have the choice you had. You met some of them, heard their stories firsthand. You helped them escape, and together you work to bring down the conspiracy you once served.<br /> <br /> <b>Unacceptable Order:</b> You were a loyal agent of the conspiracy, obeying its commands unquestioningly until the day you received an order you found you could not obey. Maybe it was a suicide mission or a doomed last stand. Maybe you were ordered to report for a dangerous new treatment or for vivisection. Maybe you were instructed to hurt someone you cared about or perpetrate an abominable crime that was a bridge too far even for you. Whatever the specifics, you either fled rather than obey the order, or you carried out the instruction but were so shaken by doing so that you left the conspiracy soon after.<br /> <br /> <b>Weary Soldier:</b> You\u2019ve served the conspiracy for as long as anyone can remember \u2014 before and after your Divergence. You have done unspeakable things in its interests. Maybe you could reasonably convince yourself that it was all for the greater good, or maybe you know full well you\u2019ve spent your life furthering the goals of criminals and villains. In any case, you tired of that life and walked away. Perhaps you went with your conspiracy\u2019s blessing and a nice severance package \u2014 or at least a retirement plan better than \u201cone bullet in the chest and one in the back of the head.\u201d Or maybe you faked your own death or carved a bloody path out of the conspiracy. Regardless, you\u2019re out. Deprived of the protection they granted you, though, other conspiracies have come calling.<br /> <br /> <b>Workplace Drama:</b> It could have started with a small conflict \u2014 a disagreement at the weekly staff meeting, a tendency to chew with her mouth open, bad taste in music. Or maybe you had an instant dislike for one another. Regardless, it soon worsened until it started to interfere with both your jobs, and eventually the sniping, backbiting, and personal sabotage attracted the attention of HR. Despite their efforts at mediation, as it turned out, the conspiracy wasn\u2019t big enough for both of you. Maybe you walked away while she stayed, or maybe you arranged a little accident that people weren\u2019t convinced was an accident after all. In any case, you didn\u2019t stick around to find out what happened next. The conspiracy is probably still looking for you, and it will be big trouble if they find you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T04:03:46-07:00","id":1536149,"title":"","content":"Today I'm previewing a bit about Touchstones and what it means to &quot;further&quot; them. The Patreon in my signature also has a free preview of what it means to Falter, including optional systems for handling those times when a Renegade doesn't live up to her own expectations (and for those who absolutely can't wait, the full text of the second half of Chapter One is available to paid members).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Touchstones</b></span><br /> <br /> Deviant souls burn white-hot \u2014 like the reactor cores of nuclear power plants. Touchstones act as coolant systems that, as long as they are functioning, leech away the excess heat of the nuclear reactions. Without them, the fire of the Broken\u2019s soul reaches a temperature that exceeds its metaphorical melting point. Unlike a nuclear power plant, however, his soul has no reactor shielding and no failsafes to shut down the reaction if it gets out of control. In the absence of steady coolant pressure, this meltdown causes further damage to the Remade\u2019s soul (Instability) and can lead to a catastrophic meltdown (the End Stage Condition).<br /> <br /> Not all Deviants rely on the same coolants or cooling systems. They have many different ways of expressing Conviction and Loyalty, and they have a wide range of options in whom (or what) they choose as their Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Self-Expression</b></span><br /> <br /> A Deviant does not need to express her hatred of a Conviction Touchstone with immediate and outright murder. Nor does Loyalty compel her to constant acts of self-sacrifice in the name of protecting her Touchstones from harm. In practice, both scenarios are rare compared to less drastic interactions.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Expressions of Conviction</span></b><br /> <br /> Deviants aren\u2019t necessarily murderers. True, they only heal major Instability by destroying a Conviction Touchstone, but even that doesn\u2019t always mean \u201ckill\u201d. Remade need their Touchstones, and killing a Conviction Touchstone at the earliest possible opportunity is usually wasteful. After all, choosing and affirming a new Touchstone takes time, and eliminating <i>all</i> the Broken\u2019s Touchstones permanently worsens their damaged state (making them Ferals). Unless the Deviant is suffering from extreme (major) Instability, small acts of defiance, opposition, and sabotage can soothe her soul\u2019s injuries for a long time. Some Remade grow so dependent on a Conviction Touchstone for their Stability that they maintain their quiet animosity for years \u2014 regularly needling, harming, or inconveniencing the target of their rage.<br /> <br /> If the Broken\u2019s actions set off a chain of events that leads to the Touchstone\u2019s death or permanent incapacitation, this still heals a major Instability, even if the Deviant isn\u2019t the one who pulled the trigger or plunged the dagger into her heart.<br /> <br /> The Deviant also heals a major Instability if he places the Touchstone into an apparent certain death situation, such that any reasonable person would presume they had died. If a Conviction Touchstone later comes back from the \u201cdead\u201d, the Broken may immediately replace an existing Touchstone (either Conviction or Loyalty) with the returning Touchstone, who is not considered Wavering, although this counts against the limit of naming one new Touchstone per chapter.<br /> <br /> At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, the Deviant may also heal a major Instability if he completely transforms the Touchstone or irreversibly destroys his victim\u2019s life. Forcibly subjecting the target to the Divergence or sabotaging her intended Divergence so that it does not bestow the desired benefits or imposes much worse disadvantages than expected often qualifies. Inflicting an injury sufficient to change the victim\u2019s personality, or one that permanently bars her from her chosen vocation (cutting off the hands of a professional pianist, for example, or destroying the eyes of a sniper) may also suffice. Certain kinds of scandal can likewise drive a politician, financier, or government worker from their professional arena and prevent them from returning to it. For some Remade, alternatively, so thoroughly reforming a Conviction Touchstone or convincing him of the error of his ways that he <i>wants</i> to leave behind who he is and make amends for his past crimes can also qualify.<br /> <br /> Below are 15 ways Deviants might express their Conviction without resorting to killing the Touchstone in question. Taking action to oppose a Conviction Touchstone should take some amount of gaming-table time to heal Instability. Locking a Touchstone in your basement and taunting (or torturing) him off-camera shouldn\u2019t count \u2014 although it\u2019s certainly something a Deviant might do \u2014 but foiling his escape attempt or convincing the cops not to come inside to investigate the screams the neighbors reported coming from your house usually will.<br /> <br /> <b>Bully:</b> The Remade gains professional power over the target and uses this position of authority to make the Touchstone\u2019s life miserable in ways small or large \u2014 from setting unrealistic goals to creating an unpleasant working environment to levying unfair punishments for perceived failures. While most bosses don\u2019t wield life-and-death power over those who report to them, if the Deviant does and he uses it to get his Touchstone killed (such as a commander who can order a soldier on a suicide mission), it can permit the Broken to heal a major Instability.<br /> <br /> <b>Dehumanize:</b> The Remade causes or forces the Touchstone to suffer some indignity. This often has a physical component (a bucket of pig\u2019s blood poured on the victim, for example) but it\u2019s primarily a psychological attack. It either makes the victim act in ways that are contrary to his self-identity (committing cannibalism, for example, or killing a friend in order to save his own life) or embarrasses him in front of either a large group of strangers or a smaller group of people he wishes to impress.<br /> <br /> <b>Discredit:</b> The Remade targets the Touchstone\u2019s professional or social reputation. Because of the Broken\u2019s intervention, the children\u2019s entertainer is shown to be a sex predator, or the academic\u2019s papers are works of plagiarism, or the preacher is caught on camera laughing at how he has fleeced his clueless flock to make himself rich. This usually heals a minor Instability, although it can heal a major Instability if it leaves the target\u2019s reputation so badly stained that he can never participate in a field or mingle in a social circle again.<br /> <br /> [SNIP]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Expressions of Loyalty</b></span><br /> <br /> Although the mere fact that the Remade relies upon them for her survival often puts Loyalty Touchstones in harm\u2019s way \u2014 forcing her to protect or rescue them \u2014 Deviants express Loyalty in many ways, any of which can restore their Stability. As well, the intensity and social acceptability of their behavior depends on the individual\u2019s personality and often how much Instability they have accrued. Broken who have few Touchstones are more likely to resort to desperate means than those with many, as are transformed who have a lot of Instability.<br /> <br /> Most expressions of Loyalty can look like perfectly healthy gestures of friendship and love. This doesn\u2019t change the fact that they are critically necessary for the Broken. The Remade don\u2019t just feel lonely or suffer mental and physical health issues if deprived of opportunities to engage with their Touchstones. They manifest increasingly terrible and numerous Scars until their powers go nuclear and kill them. Maintaining and deepening relationships with Touchstones is of deadly importance to them. Stripped of their Integrity, Remade are naturally less retrained in their behavior, so it isn\u2019t so surprising that they sometimes take things too far.<br /> <br /> Some Deviants can count on their Touchstones to initiate meaningful contact with them. Maybe her best friend invites her out for dinner and drinks almost weekly, like clockwork. Most Remade must engage in a bit of give-and-take. That same friend starts dating someone she\u2019s really into, and while she\u2019s sometimes free on the usual night of the week, the Deviant needs to make plans with her at other times to continue getting her fix. Broken who get desperate may resort to manufacturing circumstances to ensure that their Touchstones spend time with them. The Remade in the other examples, jealous of the one who she feels has taken her friend away from her, secretly sabotages the relationship or, in a worst-case scenario, kills him so that she can have her friend to herself. Oftentimes, jealousy is an expression of fear and neediness; the Deviant needs regular contact with at least some of her Touchstones and is afraid that if they forge bonds with someone else it might mean they have less time for her, or that they will abandon her entirely.<br /> <br /> Similarly, some Deviants express Loyalty with no strings attached. They give of themselves because they want their Touchstone to be happy and healthy, seeing this as its own reward. Such unconditional love can leave them open to exploitation, however. Other Deviants try to get as much out of their relationship as possible. They trust in their Touchstone\u2019s good nature or lack of less toxic relationships to ensure that they continue to meet the Broken\u2019s needs. What little they give back they use as emotional leverage to prove that their Touchstone should do more to meet the Remade\u2019s needs. Sure, he\u2019ll lend you money, but whenever you argue about anything he\u2019ll remind you of all the times he\u2019s lent you money as evidence that you should let him have his way. Most Broken need to learn to balance these two approaches \u2014 sometimes giving freely, and sometimes expecting (or at least asking for) something in return \u2014 but this can be difficult for them, especially those whose shrunken number of Touchstones and/or rising Instability make them desperate for their Touchstone\u2019s continued attention.<br /> <br /> Below are 15 ways Remade can express their devotion to a Loyalty Touchstone. Each includes both benign and toxic versions. As with taking action to oppose a Conviction Touchstone, deepening one\u2019s relationship with a Loyalty Touchstone should take some amount of gaming-table time to heal Instability. Going to bed with your Touchstone lover for the first time certainly counts, but sharing a bed with them for several uneventful weeks \u2014 and presumably having sex some of the time \u2014 shouldn\u2019t. It isn\u2019t that it must put either of you in peril or cause you significant injury (although Renegades can regain Willpower if they take risks or suffer harm in doing so), but that the event should further the story of your relationship or, at the very least, set the table for events that will threaten or alter it.<br /> <br /> <b>Accompany:</b> The Deviant participates in a social activity with his Touchstone \u2014 anything from a fishing trip or sporting event to a stake-out or heist. The key is that it gives the Remade an opportunity to share an experience with the Touchstone. This becomes toxic if the Broken invites himself along on activities when his Touchstone doesn\u2019t want him there, particularly if he stalks or stows away to stay close to them long enough to find an opportunity to insert himself into their activity.<br /> <br /> <b>Depend:</b> The Touchstone takes care of the Deviant. This can range from tending her injuries or posting her bail, to picking up after her or insisting that she take better care of herself. This becomes toxic if she intentionally puts herself in harm\u2019s way so that he can care for her when she gets hurt, or if she defers simple maintenance tasks until they come to his attention so that he can perform them.<br /> <br /> <b>Finance:</b> The Broken gives the Touchstone money or pays her way. This can become toxic if the Deviant expects to be repaid or demands some non-monetary favor in return, especially if his \u201ccharity\u201d is something that will place the Touchstone deeply in his debt and so gives the Remade leverage over her.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T04:07:21-07:00","id":1536197,"title":"","content":"Next week I'm revealing one expanded core Form (Amalgam, Self-Made, Symbiote, or Transmission) and one new Form (Allayed, Ambivalent, Dedicated, Summoner, or Transitional). I've put up a couple of polls at the Patreon in my signature, so if you have a preference, go there and vote. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T19:26:39-07:00","id":1536225,"title":"","content":"If I may ask, what's the story behind making the Dedicated Form? Genuinely shocked and interested it's a Form and not some kinda thing you'd see in a storytellers guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T19:51:54-07:00","id":1536226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536225#post1536225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask, what's the story behind making the Dedicated Form? Genuinely shocked and interested it's a Form and not some kinda thing you'd see in a storytellers guide</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like they could fill the role of minor splats in other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T19:54:54-07:00","id":1536227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536226#post1536226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like they could fill the role of minor splats in other game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but note this is a Form. So still a complete splat. I don't know, seems interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T20:07:11-07:00","id":1536228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536225#post1536225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask, what's the story behind making the Dedicated Form? Genuinely shocked and interested it's a Form and not some kinda thing you'd see in a storytellers guide</div> </div> </div> </div>There were three directions from which I arrived at Dedicated. First, the core includes numerous references to failed Divergences, including implying that some people survive but wind up with Scars and no Variations. It made sense to address those directly. Second, people would occasionally ask me why there was no &quot;half-splat&quot; in Deviant. After all, Werewolf has its Wolf-Blooded, Vampire its ghouls, and Mage its Sleepwalkers. It seemed to me that there was an appetite for an answer to that question beyond the flip &quot;a half-Deviant is just a mortal with a Persistent Condition.&quot; The more I thought about it, the more it seemed like these failed Remade were just as much victims of the Web of Pain as the Broken and had every reason to want revenge; they just lacked the full set of tools that Deviants had. Third, I've always had this vision in my head of what Broken were like before conspiracies had ubiquitous means of surveillance, and part of that was the idea that some people went on quests to encounter supernatural shit that would transform them.<br /> <br /> The Dedicated were meant to address all that. They're an advanced Form like those in The Clades Companion. Depending on the options you choose, they can range from, yes, blue book mortals with Scars (or other pieces of the Deviant template) to Deviants with a couple pieces of the template excised. If you want to play a Dedicated in a cohort of full Renegades and explore the horror and tragedy of the Divergence without all the kewl powerz, you can do that. If you want to play an all-Dedicated chronicle - whether the arc is &quot;failed experiments trying to get revenge anyway&quot; or &quot;Born not yet come into their full strength but going to get there in a story or two&quot; (literally a game I'm in right now) - you can do that, too.<br /> <br /> These aren't automatically antagonists, and while I think the Form is only going to appeal to certain kinds of players, it didn't seem like it would be a waste of 1,000 or so words to give them a way to do it. It's not like everyone wants to play a Transmissible, Symbiote, Self-Made, or Amalgam, either. So, even though they make great STCs, they go in the Player's Guide because they are characters I can envision players choosing to play, either in Dedicated-only chronicles or mixed ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T20:45:57-07:00","id":1536230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536228#post1536228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were three directions from which I arrived at Dedicated. First, the core includes numerous references to failed Divergences, including implying that some people survive but wind up with Scars and no Variations. It made sense to address those directly. Second, people would occasionally ask me why there was no &quot;half-splat&quot; in Deviant. After all, Werewolf has its Wolf-Blooded, Vampire its ghouls, and Mage its Sleepwalkers. It seemed to me that there was an appetite for an answer to that question beyond the flip &quot;a half-Deviant is just a mortal with a Persistent Condition.&quot; The more I thought about it, the more it seemed like these failed Remade were just as much victims of the Web of Pain as the Broken and had every reason to want revenge; they just lacked the full set of tools that Deviants had. Third, I've always had this vision in my head of what Broken were like before conspiracies had ubiquitous means of surveillance, and part of that was the idea that some people went on quests to encounter supernatural shit that would transform them.<br /> <br /> The Dedicated were meant to address all that. They're an advanced Form like those in The Clades Companion. Depending on the options you choose, they can range from, yes, blue book mortals with Scars (or other pieces of the Deviant template) to Deviants with a couple pieces of the template excised. If you want to play a Dedicated in a cohort of full Renegades and explore the horror and tragedy of the Divergence without all the kewl powerz, you can do that. If you want to play an all-Dedicated chronicle - whether the arc is &quot;failed experiments trying to get revenge anyway&quot; or &quot;Born not yet come into their full strength but going to get there in a story or two&quot; (literally a game I'm in right now) - you can do that, too.<br /> <br /> These aren't automatically antagonists, and while I think the Form is only going to appeal to certain kinds of players, it didn't seem like it would be a waste of 1,000 or so words to give them a way to do it. It's not like everyone wants to play a Transmissible, Symbiote, Self-Made, or Amalgam, either. So, even though they make great STCs, they go in the Player's Guide because they are characters I can envision players choosing to play, either in Dedicated-only chronicles or mixed ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn that was a quick response lol. I will say, this Form is one I definitely want to play. Perhaps mix with the transmissible, have it be a Scarred mortal with a VERY contagious Divergece he's more than willing to take advantage of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T04:38:37-07:00","id":1536246,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely looking forward to these. I've personally been interested in what happens when you've been subjected to the Web of Pain, but not (yet?) to the point of cracking your soul open and replacing Integrity with Conviction and Loyalty. In particular, when I posted my Mad Science thread a while back (link in my sig),I posited the idea that the inventors would come face to face with \u201cweird science\u201d phenomena that would take a toll on their Integrity, but in so doing leave them with the ability to invent. This was conceived before Deviant was even announced, and riffed off of Hunter instead; but Deviant is easily the better fit, and from what I'm hearing about it, the Dedicated Form goes a long way toward enabling the existing Deviant system to handle it.<br /> <br /> Frankly, my anticipated Mad Science supplement keeps on shrinking as \u201cofficial\u201d supplements slowly eat away at what it needs to cover; all that's really left is a way to adjust the Investigation rules to represent research into Fortean phenomena, and what new forms of weird science they can open up. And that's fine with me; if <i>everything </i>ends up handled by \u201cofficial\u201d books, so much the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T08:44:57-07:00","id":1536257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536246#post1536246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm definitely looking forward to these. I've personally been interested in what happens when you've been subjected to the Web of Pain, but not (yet?) to the point of cracking your soul open and replacing Integrity with Conviction and Loyalty. In particular, when I posted my Mad Science thread a while back (link in my sig),I posited the idea that the inventors would come face to face with \u201cweird science\u201d phenomena that would take a toll on their Integrity, but in so doing leave them with the ability to invent. This was conceived before Deviant was even announced, and riffed off of Hunter instead; but Deviant is easily the better fit, and from what I'm hearing about it, the Dedicated Form goes a long way toward enabling the existing Deviant system to handle it.<br /> <br /> Frankly, my anticipated Mad Science supplement keeps on shrinking as \u201cofficial\u201d supplements slowly eat away at what it needs to cover; all that's really left is a way to adjust the Investigation rules to represent research into Fortean phenomena, and what new forms of weird science they can open up. And that's fine with me; if <i>everything </i>ends up handled by \u201cofficial\u201d books, so much the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you'll want to check out the expanded Self-Made Form once it's available, as it has an option for creating new Remade like yourself that could be easily hybridized with the Launch Devoted Line Project type in The Devoted Companion. It might not be <i>exactly</i> what you're looking for, but it may be close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T15:20:35-07:00","id":1536276,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I was wondering how the Self-Made Form relates to the Autourgic Origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T22:29:32-07:00","id":1536283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536276#post1536276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; I was wondering how the Self-Made Form relates to the Autourgic Origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Venn diagram isn't a circle, but the two have a fair amount of overlap. Autourgics are probably the most common Origin among Self-Made, with Pathologicals being the runner-up, and all the other Origins combined being a fraction of either of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T21:23:28-07:00","id":1536328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536283#post1536283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Venn diagram isn't a circle, but the two have a fair amount of overlap. Autourgics are probably the most common Origin among Self-Made, with Pathologicals being the runner-up, and all the other Origins combined being a fraction of either of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self Made Born when?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:08:31-07:00","id":1536334,"title":"","content":"Definitely the weirdest of the the bunch, yeah. Most of the thought experiments I've seen for that combination have involved time travel. Even cloning tends to invite questions:<br /> <br /> Are you truly Self-Made if you were created by someone with your genetic make-up whose memories you don't share? Can you really claim to be Born if you <i>do</i> share their memories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:58:18-07:00","id":1536340,"title":"","content":"What about a genotypal that was either lost by a Conspiracy or a descendant from a defunct one who somehow becomes obsessed with uncovering their lineage and in the process catalyzes their transformation? In a sense they wouldn't have been Remade if they didn't do the work to find the right ritual or unlock the hidden genetic trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 05-27-2024, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T05:19:32-07:00","id":1536341,"title":"","content":"You're absolutely right. Not sure how that one didn't occur to me in the moment. Considerably less tortured than cloning or time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T05:40:11-07:00","id":1536343,"title":"","content":"This was an Origin-Form combination that I used in my homebrew Hawai'i CoD setting. Made a lot of sense in that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T05:53:19-07:00","id":1536346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1535783#post1535783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next excerpts won't go up until Tuesday, but I've been asked to provide a &quot;set list&quot; of Variations and Scars in the meantime, so here is that and more:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>New Adaptations</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Universal:</b> Clean, Desperation, Practical, Talented, Unbridled Passion<br /> <br /> <b>Cephalist:</b> Disciplined, Empath, Intent<br /> <br /> <b>Chimeric:</b> Attack Dog, Ferocious, Pack Leader<br /> <br /> <b>Coactive:</b> Foil, Null, Tolerant<br /> <br /> <b>Invasive:</b> Artisan, Obsessive, Reservoir<br /> <br /> <b>Mutant:</b> Evolve, Fountain, Unchanging<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>New Forms</b></span><br /> <br /> Advanced versions of Amalgam, Self-Made, Symbiote, and Transmissible much like the new Forms in <b>Clade Companion</b><br /> <br /> Allayed, Ambivalent, Dedicated, Summoner, Transitional<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Variations</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Inspired Variations (all Universal):</b> Aerokinesis, Chronological Alignment, Dream Invader, Gravity Reduction, Hydrokinesis, Magnetic Control, Sticky Filaments, Stretching, Terrakinesis, Tool Mastery<br /> <br /> <b>Universal:</b> Conjuration, Cryokinesis, Delude, Extra Appendages, Fate-Bind, Gravity Intensification, Internet Acuity, Matter Control, Occult Singularity, Opener of Ways, Plant Control, Refuge, Shadow Command, Traumavore, Vocalization<br /> <br /> <b>Cephalist:</b> Clairvoyance, Emotion Amplification<br /> <br /> <b>Chimeric:</b> Beast Mastery, Body Modification<br /> <br /> <b>Coactive:</b> Emulate, Soul Seer<br /> <br /> <b>Invasive:</b> Matter Emulation, Mechanical Transformation<br /> <br /> <b>Mutant:</b> Cursed Flesh, Gestalt<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Scars</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Controlled:</b> Aftermath, Scapegoat, Shame<br /> <br /> <b>Involuntary:</b> Asset, Obligation<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> Animal Enmity, Cyclical Scar, Evil Twin, Hubris, Lumbering, Masochism, Nameless, Noblesse Oblige, Omega, Overconfident, Reckless, Sleepy, Traumatic Memories, Undesirable, Weak Point<br /> <br /> <b>Standard Deviations:</b> Blight, Capacitor, Caveat, Cyclical Variation, Dependent Variation, Exclusive, Intimate, Naked Variation, Tethered, Twined Scars, Unreliable, Vampiric</div> </div> </div> </div>So: are the Universal Adaptations provided as alternatives to Stubborn Resolve?<br /> <br /> Are any of these new Forms something that would let me create an ephemeral Deviant? <br /> <br /> Exactly what is an Inspired Variation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Posted prematurely 05-27-2024, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T06:02:47-07:00","id":1536347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536346#post1536346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are any of these new Forms something that would let me create an ephemeral Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't this covered in the Clade Companion with the Outsider? You could give them Natural Variations and Scars that sufficiently match being an ephemeral entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T06:13:19-07:00","id":1536349,"title":"","content":"The Outsider is a Deviant who <i>used to be </i>an Ephemeral Entity (or not); but I'm talking about a Deviant who actually uses the Ephemeral Entities rules (Power instead of Strength/Intelligence/Presence; Corpus instead of Health; a Ban and Bane; Essence; Influences; and Manifestations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T06:17:41-07:00","id":1536350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536346#post1536346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So: are the Universal Adaptations provided as alternatives to Stubborn Resolve?<br /> <br /> Are any of these new</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all new. And yes, one of these Adaptations can be in place of Stubborn Resolve. Each Deviant gets three Adaptations chosen from Universal and the ones from their Clade. There's a Merit that lets you develop additional Adaptations, including limited access to the Adaptations of other Clades.<br /> <br /> The core book Forms aren't new, but the versions in <i>Shallow Graves</i> offer way more options. Want a Symbiote that sometimes takes control over your right arm? No problem. Want a Transmissible who maybe doesn't cause Divergence but is the carrier for a <i>memetic</i> disease? It has that, too. Want to play a Self-Made who learned enough from your own Divergence to experiment with triggering it in others? You can. Want an Amalgam whose memories include contact information for people who know things about stuff? Done.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspired Variations:</b> The Variations chapter starts with some advice for building new Variations, including a section on taking a couple of existing Variations, braiding them together, and adding a twist to make them feel unique. These are examples of how a Variation built that way might look, because just explaining it in abstract terms isn't going to get most people to the necessary ah-ha moment that several examples can accomplish. Aerokinesis borrows heavily from Flight and Storm-Caller, for example, but it also has a Bruising Lash effect called Breath-Stealer that causes a target to suffocate (and prevents them from speaking or crying out). Dream Invader, on the other hand, is less <i>mechanically </i>similar to Creeping Dread, Memory Thief, and Telepathy (its inspirations) but is what might happen if you wanted a single Variation that feels like the spiritual offspring of the three.<br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Entities:</b> This isn't covered, no. You could cobble something together with Relentless Suppressible Out of Phase, AnoBio, and some other Variations/Scars, but it's not going to swap out Intelligence/Strength/Presence for Power. It's my understanding that some of the other game lines offer mechanics for this (I hadn't read that section of Geist until after the text of SG was settled on) and could probably use that as a starting point, treating Variations as your Numina and/or Influences as CC suggests for Ephemeral Entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":".  ETA responses to revised questions 05-27-2024, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T06:48:29-07:00","id":1536351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536350#post1536350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Inspired Variations:</b> The Variations chapter starts with some advice for building new Variations, including a section on taking a couple of existing Variations, braiding them together, and adding a twist to make them feel unique. These are examples of how a Variation built that way might look, because just explaining it in abstract terms isn't going to get most people to the necessary ah-ha moment that several examples can accomplish. Aerokinesis borrows heavily from Flight and Storm-Caller, for example, but it also has a Bruising Lash effect called Breath-Stealer that causes a target to suffocate (and prevents them from speaking or crying out). Dream Invader, on the other hand, is less <i>mechanically </i>similar to Creeping Dread, Memory Thief, and Telepathy (its inspirations) but is what might happen if you wanted a single Variation that feels like the spiritual offspring of the three.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do Inspired Variations reduce the Variation dots needed to cover a larger suite of abilities, but perhaps without the potency? Sorry this is just so exciting. I am a big fan of Aberrant and was hoping to see ways to bring in more mechanics like Technique (Power Suites) and Power Stunts into Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T07:09:46-07:00","id":1536352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536351#post1536351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do Inspired Variations reduce the Variation dots needed to cover a larger suite of abilities, but perhaps without the potency? Sorry this is just so exciting. I am a big fan of Aberrant and was hoping to see ways to bring in more mechanics like Technique (Power Suites) and Power Stunts into Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're more about mixing and matching than about new power suites (although they enable <i>some</i> of that). However, there are a couple of new Variations that function as suites of related powers. There are also a few example Merits that expand Variation capabilities or take advantage of overlaps between multiple Variations (such as combining Body Snatcher with Shadow Selves to take control of multiple people). The final chapter has a whole system for coming up with novel uses for Variations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T07:12:16-07:00","id":1536353,"title":"","content":"This is gonna rock so hard. Everything I wanted from Deviant is finally gonna happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T08:59:41-07:00","id":1536366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536349#post1536349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Outsider is a Deviant who <i>used to be </i>an Ephemeral Entity (or not); but I'm talking about a Deviant who actually uses the Ephemeral Entities rules (Power instead of Strength/Intelligence/Presence; Corpus instead of Health; a Ban and Bane; Essence; Influences; and Manifestations).</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you expect this prospect to deal with the fact that the Ephemeral Being mechanics are not built primarily as player-facing tools (see the perennial confusion over what can be done with various Influences), the entire categorization scheme for Scars (to say nothing of many Scars being inapplicable to ephemeral beings), the narrative requirement for deviants to be entangled with the Web of Pain (see the &quot;I Wouldn't Want To Live There&quot; sidebar and the general Magnitude cost of being invisible, untouchable, and exempt from most human frailties ninety percent of the time), and the general fact of most otherworlds being sufficiently distant from a human frame of reference that having a foot in the door requires a conspiracy to have Standing on the top half of the ladder and/or a specific type of Icon (see most Irises to gameline-related otherworlds requiring individualized Keys to access)?<br /> <br /> More to the point, much as I had to make the case to a friend for not using the Automaton Form to model their &quot;Alex Mercer but with nanotech&quot; concept just because robotic technology is involved, &quot;playing an ephemeral being&quot; in Deviant can be accomplished without going whole-hog into upscaling abbreviated NPC mechanics to support PC-level systems \u2014 Geist supplying the Absent as a Dyad works out because ghosts are already supporting characters krewe creation asks you to make, but they're geographically limited to such a degree that it's directly recommended to have at least one Anchor be portable, and the Memory subsystem provides them with a buffer that's thematically appropriate to what they are. Geist <i>also</i> provides a sidebar in the Shroud section for what effectively fills the same role as Manifestation Conditions (in a game where the main magical substance is Open to ghosts), as does Mummy in its Disembodied Condition (where the title characters have an extensive support system ensuring they can at least haunt their dwelling place and their servants).<br /> <br /> What do you actually gain from squeezing the Deviant template through the Ephemeral Being system that isn't accomplished more neatly by building a Form in emulation of the relevant effects without sidetracking the drives of Conviction and Loyalty with Essence hunger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T13:18:35-07:00","id":1536380,"title":"","content":"Wondering if Summoner will allow the Deviant to 'exist' as said-summoning outside their actual body. If so, it's gonna make my Orpheus conversion a heck of a lot easier! x3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T13:43:45-07:00","id":1536381,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with Orpheus beyond what I can glean from a Google search. Are you talking about summoning the homunculus and then directing it as it wanders far from you to do things while your body is in a coma? If so, there isn't an innate effect that is exactly that. However, you could make the argument that you could take a homunculus with high-Mag Astral Travel and use Body Snatcher to monitor it and take direct control of its actions for a scene at a time. That's not going to work in every chronicle, but a whole team of telepathic Summoners sending out their avatars to wreak havoc on their enemies (or get back their stolen bodies from the Underworld) could be pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T23:09:07-07:00","id":1536407,"title":"","content":"<b>Orpheus </b>features protagonists who, because of a near-death experience, are now able to project their consciousness into the Underworld in a ghost-like form. Astral Travel as written assumes that you're ultimately going to be trying to interface with the Astral Realms (i.e., dreams); but an Inspired \u201cGhostly Projection\u201d Variation that replaces the third, fourth, and/or fifth dots with something that's more about being able to take on a ghostly form while projected, and to enter the Underworld instead of someone's dreams, would cover what's being looked for very closely. Am I understanding Inspired Variations properly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T03:41:31-07:00","id":1536413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536407#post1536407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Orpheus </b>features protagonists who, because of a near-death experience, are now able to project their consciousness into the Underworld in a ghost-like form. Astral Travel as written assumes that you're ultimately going to be trying to interface with the Astral Realms (i.e., dreams); but an Inspired \u201cGhostly Projection\u201d Variation that replaces the third, fourth, and/or fifth dots with something that's more about being able to take on a ghostly form while projected, and to enter the Underworld instead of someone's dreams, would cover what's being looked for very closely. Am I understanding Inspired Variations properly?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that the You Wouldn't Want to Live There sidebar in Clades Companion still applies (i.e., you're either playing a high Standing chronicle in which the conspiracy can still mess with you when you're in the Underworld, or you're discarding the default gameplay loop of Deviant entirely), yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T04:02:11-07:00","id":1536414,"title":"","content":"It's Tuesday and time for a new preview. Today, I'm previewing new Adaptations and the &quot;Advanced&quot; version of Symbiote, which won the poll (Summoner won the other poll, so expect to see that one on Thursday). I'm posting the new Cephalist and Chimeric Adaptations here. You can see Symbiote for free by following the link in my signature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Alternate Adaptations</span><br /> <br /> The Remade are a diverse lot, with even Broken of the same Clade manifesting wildly different abilities and frailties. Conspiracies categorize Deviants into Clades based on the apparent means by which their abilities manifest, their original source, and their Adaptations, but those with the greatest understanding of the Divergence know that all these categories are inherently flawed. The same occult circumstances can result in dissimilar Remade, while entirely different stimuli can produce remarkably similar Deviants. Adaptations, often cited as the ultimate taxonomical determiner of Clade, are not, in fact, universal to all members of each Clade. As with all things among the transformed, exceptions proliferate.<br /> <br /> Each Deviant begins play with three Adaptations. By default, these are the ones described in <b>Deviant</b> \u2014 Stubborn Resolve (a Universal Adaptation) and two Clade-specific Adaptations (one \u201cutility\u201d Adaptation and one \u201creset\u201d Adaptation). Individual Remade may instead manifest Adaptations chosen from the 20 new optional alternate Adaptations below. These must be chosen from the Universal category or those specific to their Clade, although Broken who survive long enough can partially overcome this limit through the Adaptable Merit (p. XX).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Cephalist</span><br /> <br /> Cephalist Adaptations reflect Psychics\u2019 unshakable will and awareness of the mental states of others. They are heavily dependent on Willpower to fuel their Adaptations.<br /> <br /> With so many demands on their focus, Psychics must be careful to husband their mental reserves. True, a night\u2019s sleep or a few hours spent stalking a Conviction Touchstone can restore their equilibrium, but when those aren\u2019t options the reliance on Willpower can force some very careful decisions regarding opportunity costs. Conspiracy agents will often exploit this flaw by provoking Cephalists into calling upon their Adaptations before withdrawing from the confrontation, only to attack anew once the initial rush of power has passed and left the Psychic hollowed out and vulnerable.<br /> <br /> <i>Most Psychics have the Iron Will Adaptation, which permits them to draw additional power from within by sheer force of will. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Cephalists with Focus (which is many of them) often have a larger than usual number of relatively weak Variations and either many minor Scars or a small number of more significant Scars. This is seldom a limitation when they can push those abilities to limits unthinkable to others simply by wanting it hard enough. Because the Willpower cost of affecting several Variations a little is the same as increasing the effectiveness of one or two Variations by a lot, there is no inherent disincentive to this strategy.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplined:</b> The Psychic exerts extra control over her abilities through sheer force of will. Once per chapter, the Scar Finesse of all Variations entangled with a Scar of the character\u2019s choice increases to 5 until the end of the scene; if Scar Finesse is already 5, it instead increases to 6. This does not affect Techniques. She can push this further (either upon calling on the Adaptation or as a reflexive action on a later turn during the same scene) by spending one point of Willpower per additional Scar affected by the Adaptation or to increase the Scar Finesse of Variations entangled with a Scar already affected by this Adaptation to 6. This is an exception to the normal limit of spending one point of Willpower per action.<br /> <br /> <i>Remade with this Adaptation have a reputation as undisciplined raw Psychic talents. Many have Controlled, Involuntary, or Directed Variations they can barely get to work in the first place, much less direct in a useful way, using this Adaptation to exercise a degree of finesse that exceeds anything most Broken can achieve. Others have Scars of multiple Attribute types or Attribute types with which they don\u2019t have natural faculty \u2014 such as a Deviant with high Mental Attributes but mostly Physical Scars \u2014 relying on this Adaptation to overcome the resulting Scar Finesse disadvantage when it really matters.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Empath:</b> The Broken\u2019s mind is open to the thoughts of everyone around them, particularly to those of their Touchstones, allowing them to navigate social situations effortlessly. Once per chapter, they may add two dice to all Social actions until the end of the scene. This includes any of their Variations that is contested by Composure. When taking Social actions targeting a Conviction or Loyalty Touchstone, the Psychic may instead gain the rote quality.<br /> <br /> <i>No one can get into the heads of their friends and enemies the way a Psychic with this Adaptation can. They anticipate arguments and present counterpoints woven from the doubts of those they are debating. They often know the needs and wants of those they care for before those Touchstones themselves know what those needs might be. As enemies, these Psychics are frightening. As devotees, whether the objects of their devotion love or fear them usually depends on how welcome those attentions are.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Intent:</b> The Cephalist focuses thought to a needle-thin line of white-hot plasma. Once per chapter, the Scar Power of all Variations entangled with a Scar of the character\u2019s choice increases to 5 until the end of the scene; if Scar Power is already 5, it instead increases to 6. This does not affect Techniques. She can push this further (either upon calling on the Adaptation or as a reflexive action on a later turn during the same scene) by spending one point of Willpower per additional Scar affected by the Adaptation or to increase the Scar Power of Variations entangled with a Scar already affected by this Adaptation to 6. This is an exception to the normal limit of spending one point of Willpower per action.<br /> <br /> <i>Although some Psychics with this Adaptation use it similarly to Disciplined \u2014 to cover for a weakness or to allow greater variety of Scar Attribute types \u2014 most simply call upon it for the raw strength it gives their abilities when they have the greatest need of them. The small number of Cephalists who exhibit this Adaptation in addition to Focus (and at the expense of either Stubborn Resolve or, less frequently, Iron Will) are terrors with Variations like Telekinesis that key off the product of Magnitude and Scar Power.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Chimeric</span><br /> <br /> Chimeric Adaptations reflect the Hybrids\u2019 wild natures and animal magnetism. Most draw on Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Unique among Chimeric Adaptations, Adrenaline Surge does not draw on their mental reserves, instead telling on their bodies as pulled muscles and internal bleeding. Because of the physical toll continued use of their most potent abilities exacts on them, Hybrids must be wary of when they unleash their Adaptations and limited-use Variations. Although not all Hybrids have this Adaption, most of them do. Those who lack it must be even more careful about when they deploy limited-use effects.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Untamed is the most common of Chimeric Adaptations. Deviants with it are adept at hiding their vulnerabilities when they need to, reducing debilitating flaws to barely a twinge. Most have one or more high-Magnitude Scars. Such Hybrids are notoriously difficult to track, and exploiting their known weaknesses is widely regarded as futile.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Attack Dog:</b> The character enjoys the physical advantages of his bestial side, particularly when serving his masters or confronting his natural enemies. Once per chapter, the character may add two dice to his Physical actions until the end of the scene. This includes any of his Variations that is contested by Stamina or that targets Defense. When taking Physical actions targeting a Conviction Touchstone or in obedience to an order that was issued by a Loyalty Touchstone in the current scene, he may instead gain the rote quality.<br /> <br /> <i>Hybrids with this Adaptation are the workhorses of the Web of Pain. The Devoted among them serve their masters with the loyalty of trained dogs, especially when given an enemy to target. Renegades with it are nearly as dangerous to their foes, since they have a greater storehouse of rage and no one telling them when or how they should or shouldn\u2019t direct it. Ignoring the effects of Variations, these Hybrids are unmatched in one-on-one physical confrontations with their sworn enemies.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ferocious:</b> The Hybrid is a terror in combat, inspiring panic in anyone who must contend with her. Once per chapter, until the end of the scene, whenever an opponent\u2019s attack misses the Chimeric, the next attack that attacker makes against her suffers a \u20132 penalty. Repeated failed attacks impose a cumulative \u20131 penalty until the attacker makes a successful attack against her or suffers a dramatic failure. In addition, while this Adaptation is active, the Hybrid may spend a point of Willpower to reduce an attack by a Baseline or group of goons to a chance die. The Chimeric may activate this Adaptation in response to an attack against her before the results of the attack roll are known.<br /> <br /> <i>Chimerics with this Adaptation are extraordinarily elusive in combat, evading literal hails of bullets. Although the stories conspiracy agents tell about this Adaptation tend to focus on Hybrids who also had powerful attack Variations that allowed them to cut down dozens of PMCs with barely a scratch, a Chimeric can just as easily use this Adaptation to avoid harm long enough to make good his escape.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Pack Leader:</b> The Chimeric is a natural leader. Once per chapter, as her action, she may take command of her allies until the end of the scene. While in command, she may grant each ally a two-die bonus to an action or increase a Resistance by 2 \u2014 but each ally may only benefit from this Adaptation once. While this Adaptation is active, the Hybrid may spend a point of Willpower as her action to reset its benefits, potentially allowing allies to benefit from it multiple times in the same scene. Only one Chimeric can be in command of any group of allies at a time.<br /> <br /> <i>Hybrids with this Adaptation make valuable sergeants among Devoted in the Web of Pain, and conspiracies often put them in charge of teams of operatives. Among Renegades, these Chimerics serve as a rallying point for their cohorts, leading their companions to victory against impossible odds.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T04:49:25-07:00","id":1536415,"title":"","content":"So, under <b>Disciplined</b>: \u201c<i>Remade with this Adaptation have a reputation as <u>undisciplined</u> raw Psychic talents</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T04:55:41-07:00","id":1536418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536415#post1536415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, under <b>Disciplined</b>: \u201c<i>Remade with this Adaptation have a reputation as <u>undisciplined</u> raw Psychic talents</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback. Definitely could have used a less contradictory word in the flavor text. I've added it to my list for the second proofing pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T05:08:43-07:00","id":1536419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536413#post1536413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the caveat that the You Wouldn't Want to Live There sidebar in Clades Companion still applies (i.e., you're either playing a high Standing chronicle in which the conspiracy can still mess with you when you're in the Underworld, or you're discarding the default gameplay loop of Deviant entirely), yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>A literal translation of <b>Orpheus</b> would definitely be a case where the conspiracy can still mess with you: the namesake of the game's title is a corporation that creates projectors and recruits ghosts, all for the purpose of extending their influence into the Underworld, and using that influence to extend their influence in the lands of the living as well. The initial presentation of the Orpheus corporation is as a benefactor (that is, the original game would best be modeled either as a Hunter Conspiracy or as a Devoted Chronicle, at least to start with); but it's a very shady group, no pun intended. Combine that with Orpheus' rivals (other companies that use similar tech, but with more blatantly troubling goals), and you definitely don't get to hide out in the Underworld to get away from the \u201cghost projector\u201d conspiraracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T06:14:08-07:00","id":1536423,"title":"","content":"Loving all the new content. Very excited to see what new Adaptations there will be for Mutants. Unpredictable is cool but I felt like it made the choice of Variations less interesting to a characters story. That being said I did homebrew a Merit that developed a fighting style around Unpredictable. This stuff is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T04:03:20-07:00","id":1536558,"title":"","content":"The Summoner Form won the poll, so I'll be spoiling that today. You can also check out several of the new Merits at the link below for free (full text of the second half of Chapter Two available for paid members).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Summoner</span><br /> <br /> The power of the Divergence exists apart from the Deviant or can be split off from him. This homunculus might be an ever-present, hulking guardian, an animal-shaped manifestation of pure energy he summons when he needs it, or any number of other things. It might obey his every command or twist his wishes to serve its own goals.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems:</b> By default, a Summoner\u2019s homunculus has the following traits:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Scar-Fueled:</b> Choose a Magnitude 3 Scar to associate with the homunculus (the Homunculus Scar). Bringing the homunculus into existence during a scene follows the rules for activating a Toggled Variation of the appropriate type (including the homunculus disappearing at the end of the scene) and attracts conspiracy attention as though it were an Overt Variation of the same Magnitude as the Homunculus Scar. Whether the Homunculus Scar is Controlled, Involuntary, or Persistent, the Broken carries the cost. Tribulation forces him to spend Willpower to summon the homunculus, for example, and Conspicuous Appearance makes the Remade noteworthy, not the homunculus. In a similar vein, Involuntary Stimulus causes the homunculus to summon itself whenever the Scar\u2019s conditions are met.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Assigned Variations:</b> The homunculus possesses one or more of the Deviant\u2019s Variations, each of which is entangled with its own Scar. The Remade cannot use those Variations, as they belong to the homunculus. The Broken\u2019s Attributes determine Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance, and they use his Acclimation. The homunculus does not enjoy any of the benefits of a Variation that has not been assigned to it, so a Deviant with the Enhanced Speed Variation doesn\u2019t grant the Variation\u2019s benefits to all his homunculi, nor does Superhuman Strength make them stronger. If a Homunculus Scar has Standard Deviations that limit or change how entangled Variations work (such as Target Restriction), these apply to all the homunculus\u2019s uses of Variations. Whenever the Remade purchases a new Variation, he may assign it to a new or existing homunculus instead of to himself. Adaptations can be used to reset the homunculus\u2019s limited-use Variations, but they cannot otherwise affect the homunculus.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Multiple Homunculi:</b> The Deviant can also define multiple homunculi, but each Variation can only be assigned to one homunculus at a time unless the Remade purchases the Variation multiple times to assign to different homunculi (permitted even if the Variation cannot normally be purchased multiple times). Once a Variation is assigned to a given homunculus, however, it cannot be reassigned to a different homunculus without a narrative explanation and Storyteller approval. Only one homunculus can be active at any given time.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Distinctive:</b> Each homunculus has a distinctive appearance. Although not all are humanoid (animals, machines, and stranger things are quite common), those that resemble humans have the same face, body shape, and attire each time the Summoner calls them forth.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Range:</b> When summoned, the homunculus appears at a place the Deviant can perceive within 40 yards/meters.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Actions:</b> The Deviant and homunculus each have their own separate actions, with both acting on the Deviant\u2019s initiative (unless modified by a Variation). For mundane tasks, the homunculus has six dice for actions in two areas of expertise of the Broken\u2019s choice and two dice for other actions \u2014 both of which can still benefit from Variations like Hypercompetence (treating half the appropriate dice pool as coming from its Skill) and Superhuman Attribute (adding a flat bonus equal to the Magnitude of Superhuman Attribute). Once chosen, these areas of expertise cannot change. Homunculi lack armor, weapons, or equipment when summoned. Their Defense is 3.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Other Traits:</b> Homunculi do not have Willpower, although the Remade can spend Willpower on their behalf. A homunculus disappears if it suffers any damage, although the Broken can re-summon it. A homunculus can be of Size 5 or less, as decided when the transformed purchases this Form; small (Size 4 or less) homunculi have the same advantages and disadvantages as Remade with the Miniaturization Variation, but it usually doesn\u2019t affect Health (but see Durable below) and microscopic homunculi are not permitted. Derived traits like Speed and Initiative are based on the Broken\u2019s unmodified Attributes except where the homunculus has a Variation that modifies these.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Limited Independence:</b> A homunculus has a limited understanding of the world around it. It will obey the Deviant\u2019s one-sentence/step commands (which he can issue as a reflexive action on his turn) immediately and without question, but it doesn\u2019t act of its own volition.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Undying:</b> If the homunculus is destroyed, it reforms and can be summoned again at the beginning of the next chapter, but the Broken suffers a medium Instability. If the homunculus has the Ever-Present effect, it automatically summons itself to the Summoner\u2019s presence at the beginning of the next chapter (the next scene, if it also has Easy Reformation).<br /> <br /> A Summoner can spend some of his starting Merit dots to change most of the above rules. With the Storyteller\u2019s permission, the Summoner may spend Experiences to improve the Form during play. These Merit dots can be used as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Adaptable (2 dots):</b> Homunculi can benefit from the Deviant\u2019s Adaptations, although the Broken must pay any associated costs.<br /> <br /> <b>Capable (2 to 15 dots):</b> A homunculus possesses 1 additional Magnitude of Variations per two Merit dots, although they must be entangled with Scars as normal. For three Merit dots per Magnitude of Variations, this is instead Scar-free Magnitude of Variations. The Magnitude of these Variations cannot be increased later and can\u2019t exceed 5 Magnitude total, but they don\u2019t count against the Broken\u2019s starting Magnitude of Variations.<br /> <br /> <b>Durable (2 dots):</b> The homunculus calculates Health based on its Size and Stamina (which is equal to the un-enhanced Stamina of the Deviant), plus any due to the Variations assigned to it (such as Superhuman Stamina).<br /> <br /> <b>Easy Reformation (2 dots):</b> If destroyed, the Broken can summon the homunculus again at the beginning of the next scene instead of the next chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>Ever-Present (2 to 4 dots):</b> The Deviant may summon a homunculus as a reflexive action on his turn but may not summon more than one homunculus per turn. At 4 dots, the Homunculus Scar must be Persistent, and this effect is exclusive with Limited Use, but the homunculus is always present (and counts as an Overt Scar of a Magnitude equal to that of the Homunculus Scar).<br /> <br /> <b>Far-Ranging (2 dots):</b> The Deviant can summon the homunculus to any place she can perceive within 400 yards/meters.<br /> <br /> <b>Guarded (\u20132 to 7 dots):</b> The homunculus\u2019s Defense is 1 (\u20132 dots) or 2 (\u20131 dots), or it is increased by the starting Merit dot cost of this effect (Defense 4 at a cost of 1 dot, for example, and Defense 10 at a cost of 7 dots).<br /> <br /> <b>Huge (2 to 10 dots):</b> The homunculus\u2019s Size exceeds 5 and it enjoys the benefits bestowed by the Gigantic Variation. This does not normally increase its Health (but see Durable above). The Merit cost is based on the maximum Size: 2 dots at Size 6-8, 4 dots at Size 9-10, 6 dots at Size 11-15, 8 dots at Size 16-20, and 10 dots at Size 20-25. Summoning the homunculus grants a bonus to the conspiracy\u2019s next surveillance roll equal to half the Merit cost of this effect. This effect is compatible with the Gigantic Variation, potentially resulting in a homunculus as large as Size 40.<br /> <br /> <b>Idle (\u20134 to 4 dots):</b> At \u20132 dots, the homunculus takes no action (whether independently or in furtherance of an order) unless the Remade is within summoning range of it (typically 40 yards/meters). At \u20134 dots, it takes no action except when he is in physical contact with it. If the homunculus has the Willful effect at \u20134 or \u20136 dots, Idle instead costs 2 dots for the base effect and 4 dots if the homunculus can only act when the Broken is in physical contact with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Independence (2 to 10 dots):</b> The homunculus can understand complex commands as well as an ordinary person is able to. It has greater expertise or a wider breadth of knowledge than other homunculi:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Breadth (2 to 4 dots):</i> It has two additional areas of expertise (for a total of four) and rolls three dice for other actions instead of two. At 4 dots, it instead has a total of six areas of expertise and rolls four dice for other actions.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Depth (2 to 4 dots):</i> It has eight dice in its areas of expertise instead of six. At 4 dots, this is 10 dice.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Specialized (2 dots):</i> Exchange some of the homunculus\u2019s areas of expertise for Specialties and/or Merits at the rate of five Specialties/Merit dots per area of expertise.<br /> <br /> <b>Limited Use (\u20132 to \u20134 dots):</b> The Deviant can only summon each homunculus once per chapter (\u20132 dots). At \u20134 dots, this is instead once per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Modified Scar (\u20134 to 4 dots):</b> The Homunculus Scar\u2019s Magnitude is instead 5 (\u20134 dots), 4 (\u20132 dots), 2 (2 dots), or 1 (4 dots).<br /> <br /> <b>Multiplicity (4 to 10 dots):</b> The Deviant can have multiple homunculi active, although he must still summon each one separately. Regardless of how many homunculi are currently active, they may only take one action per turn between them, although they can move normally. The maximum number of active homunculi cannot exceed two (4 dots), three (6 dots), four (8 dots), or five (10 dots).<br /> <br /> <b>Painful Bond (\u20132 dots):</b> If the homunculus is destroyed, the Remade suffers a major Instability instead of a medium Instability. This is exclusive with Painless Bond.<br /> <br /> <b>Painless Bond (2 dots):</b> If the homunculus is destroyed, the Remade suffers a minor Instability instead of a medium Instability. This is exclusive with Painful Bond.<br /> <br /> <b>Plain (2 dots):</b> Summoning the homunculus does not count as activating an Overt Variation. However, the homunculus may still attract additional conspiracy attention if it uses Overt Variations once summoned.<br /> <br /> <b>Scarred (\u20131 to \u20136 dots):</b> The homunculus has one or more of its own flaws. Choose a Persistent Scar (including Standard Deviations) and reduce the Merit dot cost of this Form by half the Magnitude of the Scar (rounded up). This Scar must be relevant to the homunculus in question and a potential burden for the Summoner. A homunculus that lacks Health cannot suffer a Scar that reduces how much Health it has, for example, and one with Conspicuous Appearance applies many of the related Conditions to the Summoner whenever he brings it forth. A homunculus\u2019s Scars generate Beats whenever they create complications for the Summoner or his cohort. A homunculus with multiple Scars uses the lowest-Magnitude Scar to calculate the base Merit dot cost and then further reduces the cost by one Merit dot per additional Scar (to a minimum cost of \u20136 dots).<br /> <br /> <b>Shared Power (2 to 4 dots):</b> The Deviant has access to the homunculus\u2019s Variations <i>except</i> when it is active or <i>only</i> when it is active (chosen when this Form is purchased). At 4 dots, he retains access regardless of whether the homunculus is active.<br /> <br /> <b>Weak Summoner (\u20132 to \u20136 dots):</b> For as long as one of his homunculi is active, the Summoner is treated as a 3-dot Retainer with three areas of expertise of his choice based on Skills in which he has at least 2 dots. Once chosen, these areas of expertise cannot change except at the end of a chapter. At \u20134 dots, he instead counts as a 2-dot Retainer, and at \u20136 dots he counts as a 1-dot Retainer.<br /> <br /> <b>Willful (\u20132 to \u20136 dots):</b> The homunculus has a will of its own, complete with its own Aspiration(s), Virtue, and/or Vice. It can and will refuse the Deviant\u2019s orders if they conflict with those goals unless he successfully strikes a bargain with it. At \u20134 dots, the Summoner must instead obey the commands of the homunculus when it is present, although he can twist its intent if he dares. At \u20136 dots, not only does the homunculus command the Summoner, its motives are so alien and terrible that its orders will almost always create problems for him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Differentiated Homunculi</span><br /> <br /> The optional effects of the Summoner Form assume that all the homunculi follow the same rules, even though they have different abilities. This is meant to keep an already complex Form from becoming too complicated. For troupes willing to accept more bookkeeping, though, a Storyteller may allow a Summoner to have each homunculus follow a different set of rules. One might be tiny and clever, while another is enormous but none-too-bright, for example.<br /> <br /> To represent this, determine a net Merit dot cost for the Form and pay that cost once. Then, build each homunculus using a budget equal to that cost. For example, a net 4-dot Form could allow one homunculus to be Capable (4 dots), while another is Durable (2 dots), Independent (4 dots), and Willful (\u20132 dots).<br /> <br /> In order to have multiple homunculi active at the same time, each homunculus must have the Multiplicity effect at the appropriate rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T05:46:42-07:00","id":1536560,"title":"","content":"Just take my money. I'm loving how this is making the spread of settings possible via Deviant between X-Men like superheroes to the body horror of Tetsuo: The Iron Man more diverse and viable. Shoot now you can truly just recreate Jojo's Bizarre Adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T05:55:59-07:00","id":1536561,"title":"","content":"The first thing I thought of when I read the Summoner was Negative Man from Doom Patrol, and Antibody from DP7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T06:44:48-07:00","id":1536562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536560#post1536560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just take my money. I'm loving how this is making the spread of settings possible via Deviant between X-Men like superheroes to the body horror of Tetsuo: The Iron Man more diverse and viable. Shoot now you can truly just recreate Jojo's Bizarre Adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been enjoying making Deviant a little less like a toolbox and more like that action movie trope where the assassin has a wall of carefully organized tools that opens up to a wall of guns, which opens up to <i>another</i> wall covered in knives, and then <i>that</i> wall opens to a walk-in closet filled with body armor, explosives and various gadgets that don't hang up on walls very well. It makes the session zero discussion of &quot;exactly what kind of Deviant game are we playing here?&quot; much more important, but once everyone is on the same page, you can do many <i>very</i> different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T07:01:41-07:00","id":1536563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536562#post1536562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been enjoying making Deviant a little less like a toolbox and more like that action movie trope where the assassin has a wall of carefully organized tools that opens up to a wall of guns, which opens up to <i>another</i> wall covered in knives, and then <i>that</i> wall opens to a walk-in closet filled with body armor, explosives and various gadgets that don't hang up on walls very well. It makes the session zero discussion of &quot;exactly what kind of Deviant game are we playing here?&quot; much more important, but once everyone is on the same page, you can do many <i>very</i> different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. I'm a sucker for things that pull from Kamen Rider and Ultraman. Seems like with the stuff you are working on I could really build out the necessary systems to do those setting tropes justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T08:14:12-07:00","id":1536564,"title":"","content":"Clarifying a bit of ambiguous wording: in the Assigned Variations rule, &quot;each of which is entangled with its own Scar&quot; is referring to the Homunculus Scar, not saying that by default each Variation is entangled with a separate Scar, correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T08:34:04-07:00","id":1536565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536564#post1536564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarifying a bit of ambiguous wording: in the Assigned Variations rule, &quot;each of which is entangled with its own Scar&quot; is referring to the Homunculus Scar, not saying that by default each Variation is entangled with a separate Scar, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's attempting to address someone who has multiple homunculi. If your Homunculus Scar for each of your homunculi is Repeatable and Controlled/Involuntary, this is kind of moot. You can make it so it always costs a point of Willpower to summon any of them, for example. But if you have four different homunculi and entangled a different Persistent Scar with each one, you're dealing with four different Persistent Scars (but at least you don't have to make a Scar Finesse roll to summon any of them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T12:47:15-07:00","id":1536578,"title":"","content":"I'm also a little confused about this bit in the Actions rule: What does &quot;treating half the appropriate dice pool as coming from its Skill&quot; mean in relation to Hyper-Competence and the dicepools in question when Hyper-Competence's effects don't have any scaling to do with Skill dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T12:52:21-07:00","id":1536579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536578#post1536578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also a little confused about this bit in the Actions rule: What does &quot;treating half the appropriate dice pool as coming from its Skill&quot; mean in relation to Hyper-Competence and the dicepools in question when Hyper-Competence's effects don't have any scaling to do with Skill dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. It may have been I meant Omni-Competence, which does. I'll review it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T20:26:52-07:00","id":1536601,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if there's a strong particular reason why Summoner is a Form and not a Variation, considering the existence of other meta-Variations like Monstrous Transformation and Sacred Flesh. It even has its own set of &quot;Deviations&quot; of a sort, which get a little more confusing to wrangle without a preexisting standard for Merit Deviations, introducing corner cases like &quot;does taking a -4 let you take up to four non-Summoner Merit dots in exchange&quot; (I assume not), &quot;can you develop a negative Deviation to Summoner mid-play and what effect does the -4 have there,&quot; and so on.<br /> <br /> It would, of course, be a very complicated meta-Variation, but it's already a very complicated Form, and I think a Player's Guide is a suitable place for a few more complicated powers anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T20:55:56-07:00","id":1536603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536601#post1536601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if there's a strong particular reason why Summoner is a Form and not a Variation, considering the existence of other meta-Variations like Monstrous Transformation and Sacred Flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monstrous Transformation and Sacred Flesh affect a finite number of Variations per instance. You can have one Homunculus that every single Variation you possess is filtered through. Forms explicitly are packages of game mechanics allowing for specific concepts that would otherwise be hard to represent \u2014 &quot;one or more of your Variations is only accessible through a special Retainer that is itself a sort of Scar&quot; isn't going to be simplified into a list like Lash's that can fit into a Magnitude 1-5 ladder of how many benefits you can squeeze in under the auspice of a concept broader than &quot;you can package multiple Variation activations into a single action&quot; or &quot;you can give the benefits of a Variation to other people&quot; or &quot;you have a particular form of attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It even has its own set of &quot;Deviations&quot; of a sort, which get a little more confusing to wrangle without a preexisting standard for Merit Deviations, introducing corner cases like &quot;does taking a -4 let you take up to four non-Summoner Merit dots in exchange&quot; (I assume not), &quot;can you develop a negative Deviation to Summoner mid-play and what effect does the -4 have there,&quot; and so on. </div> </div> </div>It's functionally the same model as the Myriad Form uses in the Clade Companion, where with Storyteller permission you can buy new qualities or buy off negative qualities as Merits. That same Form's note about negative net Merit costs is apparently meant as &quot;negative Merit costs for the Form beyond what you spend on the Form itself do not provide other benefits after character creation if they aren't spent on anything, but otherwise work like normal extra Merit dots.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T15:25:58-07:00","id":1536682,"title":"","content":"I asked my patrons if there was anything I didn't include in this week's Chapter Two previews that they though I should share as bonus content, and while folks were excited about a lot of different things, the general trend was that I should give you all a taste of Variation-specific Merits. So, here you go:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Variation-Specific Merits</span><br /> <br /> Through chance or practice, Deviants sometimes possess special affinity for a single Variation. Many use cases are covered by Techniques (p. XX), but some warrant a separate Merit covering the advantage they grant. As well, some Remade learn to blend the capabilities of two Variations into a new set of effects. In a few cases, they may even demand additional Variations, a Form, or a Scar \u2014 or else grant additional optional effects for Broken who have them. The ones below are meant as examples of these kinds of Merits, which are much more numerous than the available space in this supplement allows.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drone Master (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Body Snatcher \u2022\u2022\u2022, Shadow Selves \u2022<br /> <br /> The Deviant may attempt to affect multiple targets with Body Snatcher \u2014 to a maximum equal to the Scar Power of Shadow Selves. The Remade makes a single Scar Finesse roll that each intended target may contest with Supernatural Tolerance + Resistance normally.<br /> <br /> The Magnitude of Body Snatcher governs the degree of control the Deviant wields over each drone. At Magnitude 3, his control lasts a single turn after which he must reestablish it, and if an action he demands causes the victim to suffer lethal damage or a breaking point, he cannot affect that target again during the current scene. At Magnitude 4, he can seize control until the end of the scene, although the victim is freed if she suffers lethal damage or experiences a breaking point, after which she is immune to the Broken\u2019s possession attempts until the end of the scene. At Magnitude 5, the Broken has total control of the victim until the end of the scene, although he suffers a medium Instability if one of the victims dies.<br /> <br /> The Magnitude of Shadow Selves determines the precision with which he can direct each drone. At Magnitude 1, he can manage to guide their steps in a shuffling gait. At Magnitude 2, he can direct them to take non-violent actions that require little manual dexterity, such as fetching and carrying objects. At Magnitude 3, he can command them to engage in combat or perform other physical tasks as though they were three-dot Retainers.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prerequisite:</b> Alternate Persona Scar<br /> <br /> As an optional effect costing one additional Merit dot, the Broken may break the control of his alternate persona until the end of the scene by banishing it to a convenient vessel within range. He must successfully activate Body Snatcher and Shadow Selves, although he may usually do so despite not being in the driver\u2019s seat of his body. He has no control over what the alternate persona does with the body it has been shunted into. If the persona would lose control by forcing the victim to suffer a breaking point or an injury, it vacates the borrowed body but cannot take control over the Remade until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback:</i> When the alternate persona takes control, it may send the Remade into a nearby victim in the same way. The Deviant can attempt to reestablish control (vacating the borrowed body) but cannot do so until the end of the scene if the victim is injured or suffers a breaking point while in the Broken\u2019s care.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prerequisite:</b> Prism Deviation of Shadow Selves and Amalgam Form<br /> <br /> As an optional effect costing one additional Merit dot, the Broken may send different pieces of himself into different victims. The Deviant\u2019s victims can perform teamwork actions with him as though they were Retainers with a Merit dot rating equal to the Broken\u2019s Magnitude in Shadow Selves (excluding Deviations) and an area of expertise in whatever task the Remade is attempting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T16:59:05-07:00","id":1536683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536682#post1536682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked my patrons if there was anything I didn't include in this week's Chapter Two previews that they though I should share as bonus content, and while folks were excited about a lot of different things, the general trend was that I should give you all a taste of Variation-specific Merits. So, here you go:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Variation-Specific Merits</span><br /> <br /> Through chance or practice, Deviants sometimes possess special affinity for a single Variation. Many use cases are covered by Techniques (p. XX), but some warrant a separate Merit covering the advantage they grant. As well, some Remade learn to blend the capabilities of two Variations into a new set of effects. In a few cases, they may even demand additional Variations, a Form, or a Scar \u2014 or else grant additional optional effects for Broken who have them. The ones below are meant as examples of these kinds of Merits, which are much more numerous than the available space in this supplement allows.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drone Master (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Body Snatcher \u2022\u2022\u2022, Shadow Selves \u2022<br /> <br /> The Deviant may attempt to affect multiple targets with Body Snatcher \u2014 to a maximum equal to the Scar Power of Shadow Selves. The Remade makes a single Scar Finesse roll that each intended target may contest with Supernatural Tolerance + Resistance normally.<br /> <br /> The Magnitude of Body Snatcher governs the degree of control the Deviant wields over each drone. At Magnitude 3, his control lasts a single turn after which he must reestablish it, and if an action he demands causes the victim to suffer lethal damage or a breaking point, he cannot affect that target again during the current scene. At Magnitude 4, he can seize control until the end of the scene, although the victim is freed if she suffers lethal damage or experiences a breaking point, after which she is immune to the Broken\u2019s possession attempts until the end of the scene. At Magnitude 5, the Broken has total control of the victim until the end of the scene, although he suffers a medium Instability if one of the victims dies.<br /> <br /> The Magnitude of Shadow Selves determines the precision with which he can direct each drone. At Magnitude 1, he can manage to guide their steps in a shuffling gait. At Magnitude 2, he can direct them to take non-violent actions that require little manual dexterity, such as fetching and carrying objects. At Magnitude 3, he can command them to engage in combat or perform other physical tasks as though they were three-dot Retainers.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prerequisite:</b> Alternate Persona Scar<br /> <br /> As an optional effect costing one additional Merit dot, the Broken may break the control of his alternate persona until the end of the scene by banishing it to a convenient vessel within range. He must successfully activate Body Snatcher and Shadow Selves, although he may usually do so despite not being in the driver\u2019s seat of his body. He has no control over what the alternate persona does with the body it has been shunted into. If the persona would lose control by forcing the victim to suffer a breaking point or an injury, it vacates the borrowed body but cannot take control over the Remade until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback:</i> When the alternate persona takes control, it may send the Remade into a nearby victim in the same way. The Deviant can attempt to reestablish control (vacating the borrowed body) but cannot do so until the end of the scene if the victim is injured or suffers a breaking point while in the Broken\u2019s care.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prerequisite:</b> Prism Deviation of Shadow Selves and Amalgam Form<br /> <br /> As an optional effect costing one additional Merit dot, the Broken may send different pieces of himself into different victims. The Deviant\u2019s victims can perform teamwork actions with him as though they were Retainers with a Merit dot rating equal to the Broken\u2019s Magnitude in Shadow Selves (excluding Deviations) and an area of expertise in whatever task the Remade is attempting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is fantastic!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T17:45:02-07:00","id":1536684,"title":"","content":"Excited to see Devotion-adjacent Merits being given some attention, as &quot;use Merits to modify supernatural powers&quot; is a mechanically straightforward way to model that phenomenon if a separate system isn't used for them instead. Speaking of which, looking forward to learning about Techniques now that we've seen them mentioned in two contexts.<br /> <br /> Another couple of Summoner questions: Do Scars from the Scarred modification count as the Deviant's Scars for the purposes of entangling Variations like those provided through the Capable modification? Also, is the Magnitude limit on Capable just referring to that modification's additional starting Variation dots or does it become impossible to assign new Variations to an existing Homunculus after it reaches a certain amount of Magnitude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T18:12:37-07:00","id":1536685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536684#post1536684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excited to see Devotion-adjacent Merits being given some attention, as &quot;use Merits to modify supernatural powers&quot; is a mechanically straightforward way to model that phenomenon if a separate system isn't used for them instead. Speaking of which, looking forward to learning about Techniques now that we've seen them mentioned in two contexts.<br /> <br /> Another couple of Summoner questions: Do Scars from the Scarred modification count as the Deviant's Scars for the purposes of entangling Variations like those provided through the Capable modification? Also, is the Magnitude limit on Capable just referring to that modification's additional starting Variation dots or does it become impossible to assign new Variations to an existing Homunculus after it reaches a certain amount of Magnitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>Techniques are a few weeks off, as they're in Chapter Seven, but I'm pretty excited to show them off when the time comes. I think they'll help head off a lot of arguments at the table about &quot;off-label&quot; uses for Variations.<br /> <br /> I appreciate you pointing out the various bits of vague language in Summoner. It's a complex Form (a bit reminiscent of Relentless Variation in that way). The extra Magnitude of Variations granted by Capable are over and above starting Magnitude - kind of the equivalent of the extra Natural Variations in the Clades Companion Forms. If you want one homunculus that carries all your Variations, you're welcome to do that; there's no cap on them. I've added a it to my second proofing pass notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T04:03:32-07:00","id":1536792,"title":"","content":"This week, I'm showcasing Chapter Three, which is all about Variations. Not only does <i>Shallow Graves</i> have 35 new Variations, but it also devotes several pages to the process of designing new Variations, whether they directly borrow mechanical or conceptual bits from existing Variations as a starting point or are entirely new. Today I'm showing off one example of each: Sticky Filaments and Cryokinesis. Two more examples (Dream Invader and Extra Appendages) are available for free at the link in my signature (and as always, patrons have access to the full text of the first half of the chapter).<br /> <br /> Let's get going!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Sticky Filaments (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Overt</b><br /> <br /> <i>Tiered, Toggled</i><br /> <br /> The Deviant can fire long, sticky filaments that serve several functions.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Anchor:</b> As a Directed effect, the Remade shoots one end of the filament at a solid surface, which it sticks to. It can serve as a rope until the end of the scene, after which it disintegrates. The Broken (and others) can use the filament to climb, rappel, employ it as a belay, or even pull an object off a shelf or ledge. It is Size 1 and has Durability equal to half Scar Power (rounded up) for purposes of attempts to break or cut it. It can support the weight of most objects with a Size no greater than three times Scar Power.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Tangler:</b> The Deviant can use the filament to entangle enemies. This is a Gentle Athletics Lash (Disabling) 1 or imposes the Viscous Tilt (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 320) on a 10-yard/meter radius area within range.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, the Remade enjoys both Magnitude \u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Cocoon:</b> Used offensively, the filament is either a Gentle Athletics Lash (Disabling, Immobilizing) 3 or imposes the severe Viscous Tilt on a 10-yard/meter radius area within range.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Swing:</b> As long as his environment includes high ceilings, buildings, or other objects higher than his head, the Broken can use the Anchor effect to jump and swing from one point to another, mimicking Brachiation (Leaper) 2. This effect has the Reflexive keyword. In addition, when the Remade successfully targets one object or solid surface with Anchor, she may attempt to connect the other end of the filament to another object or solid surface in range as a reflexive action. If the secondary Scar Finesse roll succeeds, this connection is as slack or taut as the Broken wishes it to be; if unsuccessful, she chooses whether the second end of the filament hangs loose or is attached to her.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, the Deviant enjoys both Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Steely (+1 Magnitude):</b> The filament is particularly strong. When used with Anchor or Cocoon, its Durability is instead equal to Scar Power, and it can support the weight of objects with a Size no greater than six times Scar Power.<br /> <br /> <i>The Chimeric can produce strands of material that resemble spider silk but are much more durable, but other arachnids view her as either a rival or prey that they must attack and devour (Animal Enmity; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Invasive\u2019s cybernetic arm can fire various grappling hooks and nets, but it\u2019s not exactly subtle (Conspicuous Appearance; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Mutant\u2019s hair consists of extremely stretchy, sticky threads that he pulls out and deploys in various ways, but no one envies the extensive haircare routine he requires to keep it from becoming a useless tangle (Maintenance; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration:</b> Brachiation, Lash<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Cryokinesis (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Overt</b><br /> <br /> <i>Directed, Tiered, Toggled</i><br /> <br /> The Deviant commands powers of cold and ice.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Chill:</b> As an Aura effect, the Deviant may reduce the ambient temperature \u2014 but not below freezing. This creates a level 1 Extreme Environment (a moderate Environmental Tilt such as Blizzard or Slick, in action scenes) or reduces the level of a heat-based Extreme Environment by one. The Remade is immune to the effects of the Extreme Environments and Environmental Tilts he produces with this Variation. Outdoors, the radius of the cold aura is 40 yards/meters instead of 10 yards/meters.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Conjure:</b> The Remade can conjure objects made of snow and ice with a maximum Size equal to Variation Magnitude times Scar Power and Durability equal to half Scar Power (rounded up). These objects cannot have moving parts and are treated as transparent for the purpose of calculating their resistance to damage when used as cover. They must appear within one yard/meter of a stable surface capable of bearing their weight, so this cannot be used to drop huge balls of ice on one\u2019s opponents. Especially detailed or aesthetically pleasing ice constructs \u2014 or prisons of ice conjured around the transformed\u2019s opponents \u2014 may require appropriate Scar Finesse or Skill rolls, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Frost:</b> The Remade saps away the heat in a target with a Size no greater than the Variation\u2019s Magnitude times Scar Power \u2014 cooling (but not freezing) liquids or machinery. Used against a living target, it inflicts bashing damage with a weapon bonus equal to half Scar Power (rounded up) and inflicts one of the following Tilts on an exceptional success: Arm Wrack, Blinded, Knocked Down, or Leg Wrack.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, but choose two Magnitude \u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but the Broken enjoys all three Magnitude \u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Freeze:</b> As Frost (including the effects of an exceptional success), but attacks with this effect inflict lethal damage with a weapon bonus equal to Scar Power and impose the Immobilized Tilt, with the bonds considered to have a Durability of half Scar Power (rounded up). Further, this can freeze liquids solid in an instant or inflict Structure damage on objects, halving Durability (rounded up) unless the object is designed to endure extremely cold temperatures.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Whiteout:</b> As Chill, but the ambient temperature falls well below freezing, creating a level 3 Extreme Environment (the severe Blizzard and moderate Slick Tilts, in action scenes).<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, but the Deviant enjoys both effects.<br /> <br /> <i>Connecting himself with the principles of entropy, the Cephalist draws heat out of the Universe forever to produce localized areas of cold. He is painfully aware that every use of his power shortens the lifespan of the Universe by a few fractions of a second (Shame; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Coactive made a pact with ice spirits, but they are cruel and force her to share their power with those who hurt her (Asset; Involuntary; Composure).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Mutant\u2019s very presence is cold, but any environment warmer than \u201310 Celsius is hostile to their anatomy (Native Environment; Persistent).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T04:00:46-07:00","id":1536863,"title":"","content":"Time for some more Variations. Today I'm showing off Opener of Ways and Cursed Flesh. By going to the link in my signature, you can also see Traumavore and Clairvoyance for free (or full text of the chapter, for patrons). Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Opener of Ways (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Overt</b><br /> <br /> <i>Directed, Tiered, Toggled</i><br /> <br /> The Deviant wields power over doors and other portals.<br /> <br /> For the purpose of this Variation, a door is any opening that can be opened and closed, through which the Remade can pass. It can therefore include anything from an airplane hangar door to a panel covering the entrance to an access tunnel.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, the Broken may open or close a target door as long as nothing prevents it from being opened or closed (including a mundane lock). She can also sense all doors within 10 yards/meters, which is not a Directed effect.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and the Deviant may lock or unlock a target door, whether the lock is mechanical or electronic.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Erase:</b> The Broken may erase an existing door, causing a continuation of the wall, floor, or ceiling to replace it. The door reappears at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Force:</b> The Remade may create a door where there wasn\u2019t one before, provided the solid surface on which the door appears is no more than one yard/meter thick. This door vanishes at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, the Deviant benefits from both Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviation</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Occult (+1 Magnitude):</b> The Variation also works on magical doors, including portals that lead to alien otherworlds or distant places. A supernatural door opened or closed by this Variation remains so until the end of the scene unless the Deviant is defeated in a Clash of Wills. A supernatural door is considered locked if it will only open to someone who holds a special key or meets specific criteria, while one that can be opened by a password or physical manipulation of the existing space is considered unlocked. If erased, a magical door remains closed until at least the end of the chapter (and likely stays closed longer or permanently). The Broken has no control over the destination of a forced supernatural door; it leads wherever the Storyteller needs it to lead. Forcing a supernatural door more often than once per story inflicts a point of medium Instability each time after the first the Deviant does so.<br /> <br /> <i>Living things find their way into all sorts of places they shouldn\u2019t be able to get, but none can exceed the Chimeric\u2019s ability to do so when he also has Out of Phase active, although he never remembers quite how he got in (Tabula Rasa; Controlled; Wits; Deviations: Dependent Variation [Out of Phase]).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Coactive\u2019s spirit companion opens many doors to her, but it demands regular ritual sacrifices to coax it into continuing to do so (Maintenance; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Mutant\u2019s biology interacts strangely with what Baselines describe as \u201cdoors\u201d. They shut others out, but they somehow never bar his passage. He is, however, bound to respond to some passphrases in ways that rarely do him any favors (Subliminal Conditioning; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Mutant Variation: Cursed Flesh</span><br /> <br /> <b>Subtle</b><br /> <br /> <i>Discrete, Toggled</i><br /> <br /> The Broken can impose an unwelcome burden on others.<br /> <br /> This Variation allows the Deviant to impart a single Persistent Scar (including Deviations) chosen at the time she develops this Variation (the secondary Scar). This is otherwise built like Sacred Flesh (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 151), complete with options for Boons, Secretions, Tokens, and Fragments (although it does not impart Variations). The Remade may purchase this Variation multiple times, and each time allows the Broken to impose a different Scar.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, choose a Magnitude \u2022\u2022 Scar.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, choose a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, choose a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, choose a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Aura (+1 Magnitude):</b> <i>Must be a Boon.</i> The Scar affects <i>all</i> viable targets within short range, whether friend or foe.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Parasite (+0 Magnitude):</b> The secondary Scar is Controlled or Involuntary, instead, but it can only affect other Remade, adding an additional drawback to all the Variations entangled to one of the victim\u2019s Scars. The Remade imposing this curse may choose a known Scar (or stipulate that it affects whichever Scar is entangled with a Variation known to her); otherwise, it affects a Scar at random. This cannot affect Persistent Perpetual Variations.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Infection (+1 Magnitude):</b> As Parasite, but the Scar may target supernatural beings other than Deviants, punishing them whenever they use an occult ability that requires an action and/or roll to activate. This affects a single supernatural ability \u2014 either a known capability or one chosen at random.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Infestation (+1 Magnitude):</b> As Parasite, but the Scar instead imposes a new burden on <i>all</i> the target\u2019s Variations, regardless of the Scars entangled with them. If paired with Infection and used against a supernatural being who isn\u2019t a Remade, it affects all supernatural abilities that require an action and/or a roll to activate.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Long-Lasting (+1 Magnitude):</b> The target instead suffers the Scar until the end of the current <i>chapter </i>(instead of scene, as Sacred Flesh). If this Scar is applied as a Boon, the Deviant may spend a point of Willpower to extend its effects until the end of the <i>next</i> chapter, potentially extending its duration from chapter to chapter.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Randomized (+0 Magnitude):</b> Choose additional secondary Scars equal to Scar Power. Each time the Broken activates the Variation, it imposes one of these Scars chosen at random.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Versatile (+1 Magnitude):</b> As Randomized and exclusive with it, but the Deviant decides which Scar to impose each time she activates this Variation.<br /> <br /> <i>The Chimeric\u2019s bite carries a curse that will bring out a bestial side not long after (a Boon with Alternate Persona with the Bestial Deviation), but she hates using it and can only deploy it when she has Inhuman Digestion active (Shame; Persistent; Deviations: Dependent Variation, Intimate).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Invasive synthesizes a toxin in an artificial gland in their right shoulder that, if it enters a Deviant\u2019s bloodstream, causes her to destabilize if she uses her powers (a Secretion with the Parasite Deviation that imposes Unstable Variation), but the gland\u2019s waste products thin their blood (Hemophilia; Persistent).</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Mutant\u2019s hair, when braided into a bracelet, circlet, or necklace, immobilizes the arms and legs of anyone bound with them \u2014 a Fragment that imposes the Missing Limb Scar. However, the process of growing and crafting such accessories requires substantial time and effort (Preparation; Controlled; Dexterity).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T06:05:44-07:00","id":1536865,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm looking forward to is the chapter where you address how to use Variations creatively. I have a concept for a Deviant who was a man who got infected by a technovirus that turned him into something not unlike a T-1000 Terminator (the \u201cliquid metal\u201d one from the second movie); and I've been trying to figure out how to do that without it being some complex mesh of multiple Variations, where I have to anticipate each and every use that a liquid metal body could be put to; and if I overlook something or don't have enough Variations available to cover everything, tough. <br /> <br /> What I'd <i>prefer</i> to do would be to take one Variation that says something like \u201cyou can give your body the properties of a liquid\u201d, and perhaps a second Variation that says something like \u201cyou can give your body the properties of metal\u201d, and then have all of the ways that those two can be used individually or in combination flow from there. <br /> <br /> What I <i>don't </i>want to do is say \u201cthe liquid part lets him reshape his arms into the form of blades, and the metal part lets him harden them into actual blades; so I need to take the Lash Variation so that he can turn his arms into blades\u201d, and \u201cthe liquid part lets him move through bars, so I need to give him a Variation that lets him phase through solid objects\u201d, and so on. Just one or two broadly defined Variations, and a way to get creative with how they're applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T06:23:32-07:00","id":1536866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1536865#post1536865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm looking forward to is the chapter where you address how to use Variations creatively. I have a concept for a Deviant who was a man who got infected by a technovirus that turned him into something not unlike a T-1000 Terminator (the \u201cliquid metal\u201d one from the second movie); and I've been trying to figure out how to do that without it being some complex mesh of multiple Variations, where I have to anticipate each and every use that a liquid metal body could be put to; and if I overlook something or don't have enough Variations available to cover everything, tough.<br /> <br /> What I'd <i>prefer</i> to do would be to take one Variation that says something like \u201cyou can give your body the properties of a liquid\u201d, and perhaps a second Variation that says something like \u201cyou can give your body the properties of metal\u201d, and then have all of the ways that those two can be used individually or in combination flow from there.<br /> <br /> What I <i>don't </i>want to do is say \u201cthe liquid part lets him reshape his arms into the form of blades, and the metal part lets him harden them into actual blades; so I need to take the Lash Variation so that he can turn his arms into blades\u201d, and \u201cthe liquid part lets him move through bars, so I need to give him a Variation that lets him phase through solid objects\u201d, and so on. Just one or two broadly defined Variations, and a way to get creative with how they're applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter Seven has a decently long section on that (Techniques), which I think you'll find helpful for what you're describing. You can also get some mileage out of Matter Emulation, which is specifically meant to address &quot;I transform into this specific substance&quot; type powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:45:43-07:00","id":1537074,"title":"","content":"In polling the patrons, the consensus is that rather than share another Variation or two, I should share the guidelines for making Inspired Variations. So, here is this week's bonus content:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Variation Principles</b></span><br /> <br /> Designing Variations is more art than science, but there are methods that make it easier.<br /> <br /> Nearly all the Variations in <b>Deviant: The Renegades</b> and its supplements started with a high concept \u2014 the main thing the Variation is meant to do. Most of the time it ends up being the name of the Variation. Flight is about moving through the air, for example, and Pyrokinesis is about manipulating fire.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the high concept suggests several related effects. Electrokinesis, for example, is a whole toolkit in itself; its possible uses simply pile up in the mind. Other times, the high concept is quite straightforward. Carapace is armor, reducing the damage the Deviant suffers from attacks, for example.<br /> <br /> From the high concept, there are two directions you can go: You can either borrow and modify effects from existing Variations, or you can create a new Variation from scratch. You can also mix the two approaches \u2014 borrowing for some effects while starting fresh when an effect doesn\u2019t match anything in existence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Borrowing</span><br /> <br /> Variations in <b>Deviant</b> are meant to be customizable. Every published Variation offers three examples of ways it can be flavored to fit Remade of different Clades and character concepts. This works the other way around, too. If your character concept has powers that aren\u2019t covered by any existing Variation, but you see parts of multiple Variations that do things they should be able to do, it\u2019s perfectly fine to combine from each of them to achieve the concept.<br /> <br /> This is easiest when the new Variation is essentially two existing Tiered Variations twined together \u2014 a choice between two Magnitude \u2022 Variations at Magnitude \u2022, with higher-Magnitude effects building on each of the two Magnitude \u2022 effects. Even in cases where one, some, or all the source Variations are Discrete or skip around, you can think of the whole as though it were multiple Variations entangled with the same Scar.<br /> <br /> A Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 combined Variation, for example, can be built to emulate up to two Magnitude \u2022\u2022 Variations, three Magnitude \u2022 Variations, or a single Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 Variation. One of Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, on the other hand, can mimic up to five Magnitude \u2022 Variations, four Magnitude \u2022\u2022 Variations, three Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 Variations, two Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Variations, or a single Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2014 together with all the relevant prerequisites.<br /> <br /> This means that Variations that are purely a combination of two different Variations\u2019 effects won\u2019t have a Magnitude 5 effect on par with either of the parent Variations. Adding a twist to such twined Variations can be a good way to make it greater than the sum of its halves. It\u2019s also okay to have a slightly more potent effect with an inherent disadvantage beyond its Scar, such as a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Variation that grants a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and three Magnitude \u2022 effects \u2014 not a legal entanglement but far from an optimal one for a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar.<br /> <br /> Variations are limited to five distinct effects \u2014 no more than one for each Magnitude. However, nothing prevents a Deviant from having two different Variations that act as two halves of a whole. With the Storyteller\u2019s permission, a player whose character has reached the limits of a twined Variation might be allowed to split it into two separate Variations of lower Magnitude and entangled to the same Scar \u2014 following the spirit (although not the letter) of the Fused and Shifting Scars rule (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 111).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Example of Variation Creation #1</span><br /> <br /> Julia wants to create a character who can manipulate local gravity. She wants it to allow her character to fall safely, jump higher, climb more easily, and maybe eventually fly a little bit. But she also wants it to be able to make objects and people lighter or heavier, slowing them down or even immobilizing them. Her Storyteller points out that that is probably too much for a single Variation. Julia agrees and decides to start with a Variation that simply weakens gravity, twining together elements of Brachiation and Flight. She\u2019ll make one that strengthens gravity later and probably from scratch. The following Variation is the result:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Gravity Redu\u200bction (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Overt</b><br /> <br /> <i>Reflexive, Tiered, Toggled</i><br /> <br /> The Deviant can loosen the grip of gravity on herself.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Slow Fall:</b> The Remade enjoys the benefits of Flight 1 (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 119).<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Sprint:</b> The Broken enjoys the benefits of Enhanced Speed 1 (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 117).<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Balanced:</b> The Deviant benefits from both Magnitude \u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Drifting Leaf:</b> This is only available if the Remade chose Slow Fall as her Magnitude \u2022 effect. The Broken enjoys the benefits of Flight 2.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Wall-Run:</b> This is only available if the Deviant chose Sprint as her Magnitude \u2022 effect. The Remade enjoys the benefits of Brachiation (Balanced) 2 (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 114).<br /> <br /> <i>Nothing too strange so far. The Remade could take both Variations at Magnitude \u2022 with a single Magnitude \u2022\u2022 Scar entangling them both, or either of the Magnitude \u2022\u2022 Variations with a Magnitude \u2022\u2022 Scar entangled with them.</i><br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Diverse:</b> The Broken enjoys the benefits of all Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Ceiling Run:</b> This is only available if the Deviant chose Wall-Run as her Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effect. The Remade enjoys the benefits of Brachiation 3.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Controlled Negation:</b> This is only available if the Broken chose Drifting Leaf as her Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effect. The Deviant enjoys the benefits of Flight 3.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, the Remade enjoys the benefits of all Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> <i>Notice what we\u2019re doing here. By building the Variation as a combination of Brachiation and Flight, requiring the purchase of every level of effect along the way, we wind up with a custom Variation that is effectively two Magnitude 3 Variations treated as one Magnitude 4 Variation. This is really as simple as it gets. Because a Magnitude 5 Scar can entangle up to three Magnitude 3 Variations, we could borrow a Magnitude 3 effect from a completely different Variation or improve upon Controlled Negation so that it emulates one of the versions of Flight 4. However, in this case we\u2019re going a slightly different direction.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Targeting:</b> The Broken can reduce the effect of gravity on a target of a Size no greater than the Variation\u2019s Magnitude + Scar Power + 2. As a Directed effect, the Deviant grants one of the Variation\u2019s effects to a target in range until the end of the scene. Remember that targeting a Directed effect always requires an action. Inanimate objects determine their effective weight by dividing their normal weight by the Variation\u2019s Magnitude times Scar Power. A Deviant with Gravity Reduction (Wall Run; Sprint) 2 and Scar Power 5, for example could allow a 1,000-pound object of up to Size 9 to be pushed, lifted, carried, and thrown as though it weighed only 100 pounds.<br /> <br /> <i>This is the only effect that is not wholly borrowed from Brachiation and Flight, instead introducing an option reminiscent of Sacred Flesh but also very much its own thing \u2014 and one that is a potential game-changer if used cleverly. This is really all it takes to make a combined Variation feel less like two lower-Magnitude Variations entangled with the same Scar, and more like a new Variation.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T10:49:17-07:00","id":1537091,"title":"","content":"Will there be new deviations for old variations and scars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T10:52:08-07:00","id":1537092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537091#post1537091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be new deviations for old variations and scars?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was out of scope for this project, but the guidance on creating new Variations/Scars should help groups come up with their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T14:43:10-07:00","id":1537117,"title":"","content":"While both offer their own set of challenges, you believe the storytellers guide will be the more difficult book to write for? And as a fun question, whats been your favorite part of writing the players guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T17:58:01-07:00","id":1537125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537117#post1537117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While both offer their own set of challenges, you believe the storytellers guide will be the more difficult book to write for? And as a fun question, whats been your favorite part of writing the players guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're very different books.<br /> <br /> With Shallow Graves, I had the advantage of years of accumulated draft Variations, Scars, Merits, and Forms to work with. Some of those were just the usual constant tinkering I do on creative projects with no specific deadline, but a lot of them came as the result of &quot;granting wishes&quot; on the Discords. That gave a me a de facto platform for workshopping them. Even a long Variation or Form is sharable in that venue. By the time I decided to move forward with a STV Player's Guide, I already knew exactly what I was including and how many words I would likely need to flesh them out. It wasn't too difficult to stay on task or meet my self-imposed deadlines, and the ideas flowed pretty easily into the neat little jars I had prepared for them.<br /> <br /> Black Vans (the Storyteller's Guide) has always been a more nebulous and difficult to share project.<br /> <br /> First, the audience is smaller. At a guess, maybe 1 in 4 or 1 in 5 players is also a Storyteller, so the number of people who are going to be excited about material from a STG is much lower than those who would read and provide feedback on a Variation thrown together in 30 minutes and posted in the Deviant channel.<br /> <br /> Second, most STG material is much longer than is reasonably sharable on a Discord channel or even a web forum - at least not without drowning out other voices and conversations with whom I'm sharing space. The reason I ultimately decided to set up a Patreon page as part of the promotional push on Shallow Graves had less to do with establishing a revenue stream and more a matter of creating a venue where I can share long excerpts of works in progress. For now, it's all Shallow Graves all the time, but once the Player's Guide is fully live, I expect to shift the Patreon's focus to Black Vans to seek feedback that will help me refine my ideas.<br /> <br /> Third, Black Vans is more ambitious in its scope than any other CofD Storyteller's Guide that I'm aware of. I originally outlined it as being about as long as Shallow Graves (~210 pages excluding index), but I'm finding that a lot of the topics in it are taking more words to unpack than I anticipated. While this might seem like no big deal because it isn't a print book and doesn't <i>require </i>outside writers, I still have to pay for layout, editing, and art; every page of text costs around $30 to produce. That's likely to mean that either I must make significant cuts, or I need to find a way to raise more money so I can keep more of the words going into layout. How many sales Shallow Graves has (especially in its first three months) will have a significant influence on this, and patrons can also help make this a reality by continuing to support my ambitions even after the Player's Guide is available for sale.<br /> <br /> As far as what my favorite part of writing Shallow Graves was, you realize you're asking a parent to choose between their children, don't you? Or a book-lover to choose their favorite book? But I think I can honestly say that the best part of writing this book has been the outpouring of support I've had from the game's fans stretching all the way back to the Kickstarter. Without their outspoken enthusiasm for the game, their eagerness to welcome and help people who are new to Deviant, and their palpable excitement over the prospect of this project, Shallow Graves would not exist.<br /> <br /> Whenever I was feeling a little dry while writing a section and needed something to stir up my brain, fans were always willing to shout suggestions and prompts at me until my ideas were flowing smoothly again. Whenever I asked for examples of play so that I had a better idea of how Deviant is played in the wild, fans told their stories, posted links to APs, or invited me to observe (or join) their PBP Deviant games. When I needed beta readers, fans stepped up and gave me well over 100 pages of notes to help improve it. When I needed resources to help me with promotion (this is my first STV project, after all), a fan pointed me in the right direction.<br /> <br /> I love writing and would do it even if I knew no one would ever read it, but it's been so wonderful to feel like I also have an appreciative audience. It makes the hundreds of hours I've spent writing, revising, and thinking about this project feel all the more worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T14:38:35-07:00","id":1537161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537125#post1537125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're very different books.<br /> <br /> With Shallow Graves, I had the advantage of years of accumulated draft Variations, Scars, Merits, and Forms to work with. Some of those were just the usual constant tinkering I do on creative projects with no specific deadline, but a lot of them came as the result of &quot;granting wishes&quot; on the Discords. That gave a me a de facto platform for workshopping them. Even a long Variation or Form is sharable in that venue. By the time I decided to move forward with a STV Player's Guide, I already knew exactly what I was including and how many words I would likely need to flesh them out. It wasn't too difficult to stay on task or meet my self-imposed deadlines, and the ideas flowed pretty easily into the neat little jars I had prepared for them.<br /> <br /> Black Vans (the Storyteller's Guide) has always been a more nebulous and difficult to share project.<br /> <br /> First, the audience is smaller. At a guess, maybe 1 in 4 or 1 in 5 players is also a Storyteller, so the number of people who are going to be excited about material from a STG is much lower than those who would read and provide feedback on a Variation thrown together in 30 minutes and posted in the Deviant channel.<br /> <br /> Second, most STG material is much longer than is reasonably sharable on a Discord channel or even a web forum - at least not without drowning out other voices and conversations with whom I'm sharing space. The reason I ultimately decided to set up a Patreon page as part of the promotional push on Shallow Graves had less to do with establishing a revenue stream and more a matter of creating a venue where I can share long excerpts of works in progress. For now, it's all Shallow Graves all the time, but once the Player's Guide is fully live, I expect to shift the Patreon's focus to Black Vans to seek feedback that will help me refine my ideas.<br /> <br /> Third, Black Vans is more ambitious in its scope than any other CofD Storyteller's Guide that I'm aware of. I originally outlined it as being about as long as Shallow Graves (~210 pages excluding index), but I'm finding that a lot of the topics in it are taking more words to unpack than I anticipated. While this might seem like no big deal because it isn't a print book and doesn't <i>require </i>outside writers, I still have to pay for layout, editing, and art; every page of text costs around $30 to produce. That's likely to mean that either I must make significant cuts, or I need to find a way to raise more money so I can keep more of the words going into layout. How many sales Shallow Graves has (especially in its first three months) will have a significant influence on this, and patrons can also help make this a reality by continuing to support my ambitions even after the Player's Guide is available for sale.<br /> <br /> As far as what my favorite part of writing Shallow Graves was, you realize you're asking a parent to choose between their children, don't you? Or a book-lover to choose their favorite book? But I think I can honestly say that the best part of writing this book has been the outpouring of support I've had from the game's fans stretching all the way back to the Kickstarter. Without their outspoken enthusiasm for the game, their eagerness to welcome and help people who are new to Deviant, and their palpable excitement over the prospect of this project, Shallow Graves would not exist.<br /> <br /> Whenever I was feeling a little dry while writing a section and needed something to stir up my brain, fans were always willing to shout suggestions and prompts at me until my ideas were flowing smoothly again. Whenever I asked for examples of play so that I had a better idea of how Deviant is played in the wild, fans told their stories, posted links to APs, or invited me to observe (or join) their PBP Deviant games. When I needed beta readers, fans stepped up and gave me well over 100 pages of notes to help improve it. When I needed resources to help me with promotion (this is my first STV project, after all), a fan pointed me in the right direction.<br /> <br /> I love writing and would do it even if I knew no one would ever read it, but it's been so wonderful to feel like I also have an appreciative audience. It makes the hundreds of hours I've spent writing, revising, and thinking about this project feel all the more worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow i didnt expect such a substantial answer! Thank for sharing, and your ambition is admirable. I hope you get the support needed to do that amount of work you want to accomplish, i know ill be supporting it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T04:00:56-07:00","id":1537199,"title":"","content":"Today, I'm offering a sneak peek at Chapter Four, which explores and provides many new examples of Scars and Standard Deviations. Below are Lumbering, Overconfident, and Caveat. You can also see Shame, Sleepy, and Vampiric for free at the link in my signature (or full text of the chapter, for patrons).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Persistent Scar: Lumbering (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Physical; Subtle<br /> <br /> The Deviant is slow and heavy, making it easy for enemies to run circles around him.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, the Remade suffers a penalty to Initiative and Speed equal to the Magnitude of this Scar. In addition, the Broken\u2019s player may accept a Beat whenever being slow and heavy creates a complication for him or his cohort. This can include choosing to fail rolls related to stealth, jumping, or running, as well as those related to climbing or balancing on objects that are not strong enough to bear his weight.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Heavy:</b> The Deviant is significantly heavier and denser than a human being. He sinks like a stone in water, and ordinary ropes, ladders, scaffolding, and other supports will not bear his weight unless their Durability exceeds half the Scar\u2019s Magnitude (rounded up). Others\u2019 attempts to lift, carry, drag, or give a hand up to the Remade suffer a penalty equal to the Magnitude of this Scar unless using engineering principles to do so (systems of pulleys, block and tackle, counterweights, etc.); even so, relevant Build Equipment actions still suffer a reduced penalty equal to half the Scar\u2019s Magnitude (rounded up).<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Ponderous:</b> Opponents may dodge the transformed\u2019s attacks even if they have already taken an action during the current turn, and doing so does not take up their action for the turn. They also enjoy half their Defense (rounded up) against those of the Deviant\u2019s attacks that would normally ignore Defense unless some other circumstance would deprive them of Defense (such as a successful ambush).<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Slow:</b> The Remade halves his Speed (rounded up) after applying the penalty levied by the Magnitude \u2022 effect and suffers a penalty to his Defense equal to half the Scar\u2019s Magnitude (rounded up).<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but choose two of the options.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, but all three effects apply.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, but the Broken is incapable of movement except by means of an apparatus or vehicle designed to lift, pull, or carry large, heavy objects \u2014 such as a heavy pickup, semi-trailer, or cargo plane. Most consumer vehicles like cars and light trucks will suffer serious damage if they haul the Deviant more than a short distance. Build Equipment extended actions meant to move the Remade suffer a penalty equal to the Scar\u2019s Magnitude (rather than half Magnitude).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Persistent Scar: Overconfident (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mental, Social; Subtle<br /> <br /> The Deviant has a high opinion of his aptitude in social situations that may or may not have any basis in reality.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, the Remade tends to insert himself into social situations he doesn\u2019t understand and where he may not be welcome, to interrupt or take over the role of social leader even if he is not as qualified as others in the room. Whenever this creates a complication for him or his cohort, he takes a Beat.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Foot-in-Mouth:</b> The Broken tends not to stop when he\u2019s ahead. Once per chapter, when the Deviant succeeds on a Social roll, the Storyteller may offer a Beat to force the Remade to reroll the Social roll with the same dice pool and take the second result.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Loudmouth:</b> Once per chapter, when another character would speak first in a delicate social situation, the Storyteller may offer a Beat for the Broken to speak first, particularly if he is not the best mouthpiece in the current situation. He can only refuse by succeeding on a Scar Resistance roll. If using Cohort Static (p. XX), he must bid at least one point of Static in a decision point and may do so even if it puts him in Static debt.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Balanced:</b> The Deviant suffers both Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effects. The Storyteller may only invoke one of the effects per chapter.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Keep Digging:</b> The Remade must have chosen Foot-in-Mouth as his Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effect. If the reroll imposed by Foot-in-Mouth is a failure, it is instead a dramatic failure for which the Broken does not take an additional Beat.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Blowhard:</b> The Deviant must have chosen Loudmouth as his Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effect. Once per chapter, when an ally succeeds on a Social roll when the Remade is involved in the scene, the Storyteller may offer a Beat for the Broken to interrupt, taking control of the interaction. The Deviant makes the Social roll instead. The Remade may only refuse this compulsion by succeeding on a Scar Resistance roll. If using Cohort Static, he must continue bidding in a decision point until the proposal he is supporting wins out or until he runs out of Static.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, the Broken suffers all Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 effects. The Storyteller may only invoke one effect of this Scar per chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Misread (+1 Magnitude):</b> The Remade regularly misreads social situations, often believing he is in a position of greater influence than turns out to be the case. The Storyteller may roll the Broken\u2019s Social rolls in secret, applying any bonuses and penalties without revealing what they are or announcing the result.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Standard Deviation: Caveat</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Scar Type:</b> Any<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Magnitude:</b> The entangled Variation carries a significant limitation in how it works, beyond the scope of its Scar or another Deviation. The armor provided by Carapace might afford no protection against silver-plated weapons, for example, or Telepathy might be impossible against a target wearing a hat or helmet. This restriction can often resemble those imposed by Power Failure, but this Deviation allows the Remade to add a further, automatic restriction to a Variation over and above its normal Scar. The restriction is likely to come into play approximately once per chapter, and each time it does so in a way that inconveniences her or her cohort, the Deviant takes a Beat.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Minor (\u22121 Magnitude):</b> As the base effect, but the restriction is largely cosmetic or only comes into play rarely (approximately once per story). Rapid Healing might be ineffective against wounds delivered by an enchanted sword, for example, or vermin spirits might be invisible to a spirit-detecting Specialized Sense. This is exclusive with Major.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Major (+1 Magnitude):</b> As the base effect, but the restriction prevents the Broken from benefiting from the Variation except under unusual circumstances (approximately once per story). A Carapace might <i>only</i> protect from silver-plated weapons, for example, or Bioluminescence might only function in the presence of the undead. This is exclusive with Minor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T08:15:57-07:00","id":1537205,"title":"","content":"Caveat's a welcome addition to be sure, and it's funny to me that Vampiric is the Deviation to use for &quot;you need a team of assistants to use this power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lumbering does make me wonder: what's the threshold for Magnitude 1 Scars having mechanical effects beyond Beat generation? Obviously a -1 to Speed and Initiative isn't huge, and Conspicuous Appearance 1 adds a die to conspiracy surveillance rolls by virtue of that Scar's overarching effect, but I'm curious where the line is drawn in terms of effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T08:21:09-07:00","id":1537206,"title":"","content":"Did we ever see rules for objects or locations with Variations? Concept just popped into my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T08:28:40-07:00","id":1537207,"title":"","content":"Clade Companion has rules for Prototypes, which are objects with Variations. I don't think there's anything official for locations with Variations, though I could see extending the aforementioned Prototypes rules by means of architecture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T09:00:20-07:00","id":1537208,"title":"","content":"I am eager to get my hands on the Clades Companion later this week. For whatever reason Youtube thinks I want to watch old clips from LOST, and it's giving me real Deviant vibes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T13:41:50-07:00","id":1537214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537205#post1537205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lumbering does make me wonder: what's the threshold for Magnitude 1 Scars having mechanical effects beyond Beat generation? Obviously a -1 to Speed and Initiative isn't huge, and Conspicuous Appearance 1 adds a die to conspiracy surveillance rolls by virtue of that Scar's overarching effect, but I'm curious where the line is drawn in terms of effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always a fair amount of ST discretion. I go into it quite deeply in Chapter Five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T14:34:21-07:00","id":1537217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537207#post1537207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clade Companion has rules for Prototypes, which are objects with Variations. I don't think there's anything official for locations with Variations, though I could see extending the aforementioned Prototypes rules by means of architecture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a case could also be made for using an Agent Icon to provide access to Variations to the agents of its attached Node, with Scars and Deviations limiting its effectiveness outside the location of the Node in question, but admittedly I'm not sure what &quot;locations with Variations&quot; would entail beyond &quot;place that gives you access to Variations.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T04:06:22-07:00","id":1537297,"title":"","content":"First off, <i>Clades Companion</i> is now available for sale, so <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/480383/the-clades-companion\" target=\"_blank\">go check that out</a> if you haven't already.<br /> <br /> Chapter One explored the Deviant experience in broad terms \u2014 discussing Origins, Clades, and what all Remade gain and lose as part of the Divergence. Chapter Five discusses specific Broken characters \u2014 how to create them and how to use their Variations and Scars to guide roleplaying. The sample below is from a section on the initial process of thinking about the character you want to make, whether you start from who they are (or were), what capabilities they have, their vulnerabilities, or their relationships. This excerpt only covers the first &quot;corner&quot; of the puzzle of making a Renegade.<br /> <br /> Follow the link in my signature for an excerpt from a section of the chapter about the practical considerations of character design within a roleplaying game (as well as the full text of Chapter Five for patrons).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:26px\">Starting Points</span><br /> <br /> <b>Deviant: The Renegades</b> offers tremendous flexibility in the kinds of characters that can be built using its systems. The sheer number of Variations, Scars, and Standard Deviations it puts into players\u2019 hands can be a bit overwhelming, however, and the additional examples in Chapters Three and Four of this book are unlikely to reduce the potential for analysis paralysis. Add in Merits, Adaptations, and Forms to all that, and it\u2019s a lot to take in.<br /> <br /> So, if you\u2019re sitting there with a blank character sheet, the 345-page core book, possibly two Kickstarter supplements (<b>The Clades Companion</b> and <b>The Devoted Companion</b>), and now <i>this</i>, it\u2019s normal to have a hard time knowing where to start. The purpose of this section is to help you get started, to resist the urge to focus on the giant pile of jigsaw puzzle pieces on your table and instead to concentrate on finding just one corner and some edges. Start from whichever of the four corners inspires you most.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">First Corner: Origin</span><br /> <br /> Start at the beginning \u2014 not with your character\u2019s Origin but with her origin. Who was she before her first encounter with the Web of Pain?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Childhood</span><br /> <br /> You can start at the very beginning if you want. Think about her childhood. What was her home life like, her school life? Who were her friends, and did she have any noteworthy rivals or enemies among her peers? How did she spend her free time? Was she active in sports, performance arts, or clubs? Did she have favorite books, TV shows, or movies? When the grown-ups in her life praised her, which of her personality traits did they tend to highlight? When they criticized her, what faults did they tell her were holding her back? How far did she get in school; did she drop out of high school, or did she collect post-graduate degrees like other people collect shoes?<br /> <br /> What did she dream her life would be like when she grew up? Did she have grand schemes or ordinary hopes? Did her vision of her future drive her constantly, or did she sort of expect that it would all come together when the time was right? Did these dreams play to her natural strengths or reflect a hope that one day she could overcome her weaknesses? Or did she have impossible dreams \u2014 fantasies of attaining superhuman abilities or irrational fears of suffering life-changing injuries or developing debilitating medical conditions?<br /> <br /> If she was always entangled in the Web of Pain, what was that life like and how did it shape the adult she became (or is still becoming)? While this often describes Genotypals, it\u2019s possible for someone to grow up in a conspiracy without anyone expecting her to Diverge.<br /> <br /> <b>Why We Ask:</b> Childhood can set into motion the whole course of a person\u2019s life, especially when the Web of Pain gets involved. A child with a rare disease may attract the attention of a conspiracy that promises a cure, while one born into a conspiracy might be enmeshed in its schemes from birth. A child with grand plans might make her winding way into an existing conspiracy or discover a means of triggering Divergence in herself or others. One who hoped for a quiet life could find those hopes dashed by conspiracy agents who lure or abduct her. A child\u2019s caretakers could enroll her in research studies \u2014 whether because they want to support the advancement of science, because they think these treatments will save their child or make her life better, or because the conspiracy offered them something they didn\u2019t want (or perhaps didn\u2019t dare) to refuse. Knowing what your character had (or lacked) as a child \u2014 a home, friends, family, a dog, talents, and hopes for the future \u2014 can help inform what the Divergence will take from (or give to) her.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Adulthood</span><br /> <br /> Consider who she was as an adult \u2014 whether as a follow-up to the questions of childhood, as a prelude to her collision with the conspiracy, or both. What was her day-to-day life like? How did she earn a living? If she didn\u2019t live alone, who were the other members of her household \u2014 her parents (or grandparents), a spouse and/or kids, a lover, one or more roommates, or a community united by a religious or spiritual connection? Where did she live, in the sense of both city/town/wilderness and house/apartment/compound? How did she spend her non-working hours? Did she have notable hobbies, close friends, or preferred forms of entertainment? How did she unwind?<br /> <br /> Was her life on a general incline \u2014 with a bright future just up ahead? Or was she stuck in a slow (or steep) downward spiral? Or did it vary with the day or with what part of her life you were looking at? Maybe she had it all together at work, but her home life was a mess \u2014 or the reverse. Was she generally happy or dissatisfied with the way her life had turned out?<br /> <br /> Did she have any entanglements or problems that might have left her vulnerable to the conspiracy. Was she in over her head in debt? Did she have dangerous enemies (or friends)? Was she recently diagnosed with a terminal illness, or has she been living with a chronic illness for years that she would risk much to free herself from?<br /> <br /> <b>Why We Ask:</b> It isn\u2019t unusual for people in the world of the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> to encounter conspiracy agents. It <i>is</i> unusual for these encounters to lead to the Divergence. The conspiracies aren\u2019t interested in everyone. Some are picky about their subjects because it increases the odds of success. Most are picky because they don\u2019t want to attract too much attention to themselves. Conspiracies seek out people who are vulnerable, who won\u2019t be missed, or who are desperate. Knowing your character\u2019s circumstances can inform potential vectors for the Web of Pain to ensnare her. Knowing what she had (or lacked) sets up opportunities to contrast that with what the Divergence took from or gave to her. Friends, family members, colleagues, and rivals often make good starting Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Divergence</span><br /> <br /> Consider who she became after her Divergence, including who she is now. You can treat this as a follow-up to the prior two life stages or use it as a starting point in its own right. Maybe knowing how she survives from day to day is more important to you than knowing how she got there. You can fill that in later in the character creation process or reveal it in a series of flashbacks after the chronicle begins. Nothing says you need to know everything about your character\u2019s past before the first chapter; you would be in good company with many of the media inspirations for <b>Deviant</b>. A little later in this supplement, we\u2019ll talk about how to draw Deviants together into a cohort, but for now, think of your character in isolation.<br /> <br /> Who is or was her Progenitor? How did they trigger her Divergence? Were there other test subjects, and what happened to them? How long did she stay with the conspiracy? Why and how did she leave? How has she avoided falling back into their hands (or those of other conspiracies)? How does she survive from day to day, meeting basic needs like food, shelter, and clothing? How does she stave off Instability? Does she hold her Loyalty Touchstones close, or does she keep them at arm\u2019s length for their own protection?<br /> <br /> <b>Why We Ask:</b> The Divergence is the bright line drawn between Baseline and Broken. It\u2019s natural to focus on it and its immediate aftermath. That brief period in a Deviant\u2019s life is one where she is likely to form bonds with most of her future Conviction Touchstones, and many Remade also forge bonds with people who will become crucial Loyalty Touchstones. The Divergence brings unbreakable friendships and unquenchable rivalries and animosities. How your character responded to her newly discovered Variations and Scars reflects who she was \u2014 with all masks torn aside \u2014 and speaks volumes about who she is now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Bottom Line</span><br /> <br /> Starting character creation with a deep examination of their Baseline life makes it easier to think of them as a person first and a Deviant second. It tends to draw attention to how the Divergence changed them \u2014 not just by giving them Variations and Scars but by upending their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T04:58:03-07:00","id":1537300,"title":"","content":"Okay; so this excerpt gives us \u201corigin\u201d (or rather, \u201clifepath\u201d) as the first corner to start with: taking significant points on your character's development timeline (childhood, adulthood, and the Divergence) and fleshing them out. Personally, I would also use Childhood to explore the Remade's family, and Adulthood to explore their friends and enemies, providing possible candidates for Loyalty and Conviction anchors once the Divergence happens. <br /> <br /> In your Patreon, you've provided a second corner to work from (of is it an edge to work along?) in the form of what kinds of activities the Remade often engage in, and how your character fits into each. Could you tell us, without spelling out all of the details, what other \u201ccorners\u201d and \u201cedges\u201d you identify for framing the jigsaw puzzle of character creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T05:02:17-07:00","id":1537301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537300#post1537300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay; so this excerpt gives us \u201corigin\u201d (or rather, \u201clifepath\u201d) as the first corner to start with: taking significant points on your character's development timeline (childhood, adulthood, and the Divergence) and fleshing them out. Personally, I would also use Childhood to explore the Remade's family, and Adulthood to explore their friends and enemies, providing possible candidates for Loyalty and Conviction anchors once the Divergence happens.<br /> <br /> In your Patreon, you've provided a second corner to work from (of is it an edge to work along?) in the form of what kinds of activities the Remade often engage in, and how your character fits into each. Could you tell us, without spelling out all of the details, what other \u201ccorners\u201d and \u201cedges\u201d you identify for framing the jigsaw puzzle of character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The full list of corners is origin, capabilities (often Variations but potentially Skills, Merits, Forms, etc. - and the Busied Hands section is here), Scars (which can include the negative aspects of some Forms), and connections (which is very often Touchstones and/or conspiracy). So, if it seems strange that I'm not exploring Touchstones in adulthood and Divergence, it's because they're part of another category. These all fit together, ultimately (thus the puzzle metaphor), but that's the way I ended up sorting them in this chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T04:25:21-07:00","id":1537478,"title":"","content":"For this week's bonus content, I'm giving you sneak peeks of a few more Scars - Scapegoat, Hubris, and Noblesse Oblige:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Controlled Scar: Scapegoat (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Social; Subtle<br /> <br /> The Deviant\u2019s presence has a deleterious effect on the ones he cares about.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, choose a Persistent Scar with a Magnitude equal to the Magnitude of Scapegoat (the secondary Scar). When the Remade activates the entangled Variation in the presence of a Loyalty Touchstone, that Touchstone suffers the effects of the secondary Scar until the end of the chapter unless the Broken succeeds on a Scar Resistance roll. The maximum number of victims the secondary Scar can affect at a time cannot exceed (6 \u2013 Scar Resistance). The Scar must be one that can meaningfully affect a Baseline. If the Scar has no viable victims to target in the current scene, Scapegoat gains the Bystander Deviation below.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Cohort:</b> The secondary Scar also affects members of the Deviant\u2019s cohort.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Enduring:</b> The secondary Scar plagues the victim longer, lasting until the end of the story. If paired with the Bystander Deviation, it is usually permanent.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Persistent:</b> In addition to taking effect when the entangled Variation is active, up to once per chapter, at a time of the Storyteller\u2019s choosing, it imposes its secondary Scar even when the Variation isn\u2019t active.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Sympathetic:</b> The secondary Scar can fall upon a target who isn\u2019t present in the current scene.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but choose two Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but choose three Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but the Deviant suffers from all four Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bystander (+0 Magnitude):</b> The secondary Scar doesn\u2019t affect Loyalty Touchstones. Instead, it affects innocent bystanders (Baselines who are not Conviction Touchstones, Loyalty Touchstones, or enemies). However, the Broken does not have the option to make a Scar Resistance roll to suppress this effect and Scapegoat becomes an Overt Scar. If no viable bystanders are present, the Variation works normally but no one suffers the secondary Scar.<br /> <br /> <b>Random (+0 Magnitude):</b> Choose a number of potential secondary Scars equal to 1 + Scar Magnitude. Whenever you impose a secondary Scar due to Scapegoat, randomly select which one affects the victim at random.<br /> <br /> <b>Cruel (+1 Magnitude):</b> As Random and exclusive with it and with Merciful, but the Storyteller chooses which secondary Scar to impose, and it seems calculated to maximize the Deviant\u2019s anguish.<br /> <br /> <b>Merciful (\u20131 Magnitude):</b> As Random and exclusive with it and with Cruel, but the Broken\u2019s player decides which secondary Scar to impose.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Persistent Scar: Hubris (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mental, Social; Subtle<br /> <br /> The Broken is certain he\u2019s the smartest one in the room and that there is no problem that his intelligence and Variations can\u2019t overcome if he puts his mind to it. Moreover, he wants everyone else to know it.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, the Deviant is prone to gloat over his successes (and any enemies in his power), to brag about his intelligence and Variations, and to talk about his plans even to enemies. Whenever this causes a complication for the Remade or his cohort, he takes a Beat.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Brag:</b> Whenever someone asks the Broken about himself, he must make a successful Scar Resistance roll to resist the urge to openly hint either at his Variations, his shocking plans for the future, or his past crimes. At this Magnitude, he need not be blunt or specific \u2014 particularly if doing so in present company is a bad idea, such as when he is being interrogated by the police \u2014 but anyone reading between the lines should be able to glean enough information from his not-quite-confession to pursue further lines of inquiry.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Toy:</b> Whenever the Deviant has an enemy in his power \u2014 whether because they surrendered or were incapacitated \u2014 he must make a successful Scar Resistance roll in order to kill them or let them die. If he lets them live, he cannot simply keep them prisoner or hand them over to someone else. He must either give them an opportunity to win their freedom (which need not be fair but must not assure their failure) or contrive a satisfying and elaborate method of execution that incidentally gives them a chance to escape. This does not affect the Broken\u2019s ability or willingness to kill a Conviction Touchstone out of hand.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, and choose one:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Balanced:</b> The Deviant suffers both Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Boast:</b> The Remade must have chosen Brag as his Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effect. As Brag, but the Broken can\u2019t roll to resist at least hinting about his secrets. Moreover, if asked direct questions about any of the secret topics, he must make a successful Scar Resistance roll or lay out the truth in excruciating detail even when doing so is a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Gloat:</b> The Deviant must have chosen Toy as his Magnitude \u2022\u2022 effect. The Remade\u2019s enemies are so far beneath his notice that they don\u2019t even warrant him killing them anymore. The Toy effect now applies to his Conviction Touchstones. Additionally, the Broken doesn\u2019t even toy with lesser enemies, instead freeing them a short while later, usually after regaling them with lengthy monologues meant to impress upon them how intelligent and powerful he is.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, the Deviant suffers from all three Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Calling Card (+1 Magnitude):</b> The Remade feels compelled to take trophies or leave a calling card whenever he makes a significant accomplishment. Choose an appropriate type of calling card or trophy; failing to leave/take this when the opportunity arises inflicts a minor Instability on the Broken. A calling card makes it easier for the conspiracy (or the authorities) to identify his handiwork; leaving a calling card makes this Scar count as Overt for the conspiracy\u2019s next surveillance roll. A trophy makes it easier for the Broken\u2019s crimes to be traced to him; if investigators gain access to his trophy collection, he suffers the Hunted Condition.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Persistent Scar: Noblesse Oblige (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mental, Social; Subtle<br /> <br /> The Broken suffers a supernatural compulsion to fulfill the desires of strangers.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022, the Deviant\u2019s player may accept a Beat whenever she performs a random act of kindness for a stranger that results in a complication for her or her cohort.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and up to once per chapter the Storyteller may choose a character the Remade is compelled to help. The Deviant must ensure that the target fulfills a Vice, Virtue, Aspiration, or esoteric drive (such as furthering a Touchstone). The Remade knows which person is her target but doesn\u2019t automatically receive knowledge of his desires; she needs to learn that information on her own. Unless the target accomplishes his goal before the end of the <i>next</i> chapter, the Deviant suffers one of the following at the beginning of the following chapter, chosen at the time she develops this Scar:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Health:</b> The Remade suffers a point of lethal damage that cannot be healed by supernatural effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Power:</b> This Scar becomes Controlled instead of Persistent and gains the Repeatable keyword. The Deviant cannot activate the entangled Variations unless she has fulfilled the obligation since the beginning of the <i>previous</i> chapter.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Stability:</b> The Broken suffers a minor Instability.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Will:</b> The Deviant loses a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> If the Storyteller chooses a new target, it frees the Remade from any existing obligation (and potential consequences for failing to uphold it).<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but the Broken has fewer avenues by which to satisfy her compulsion. Choose two of the following when the Deviant develops this Scar, and helping the target fulfill these no longer satisfies the conditions of this Scar: Esoteric, Short-Term Aspiration, Long-Term Aspiration, Vice, or Virtue.<br /> <br /> At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, but only one type of desire satisfies the conditions of this Scar.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> <br /> Except for Compelled, all the below Deviations are only allowed if the base effect is Magnitude \u2022\u2022 or higher.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Guided (\u20131 Magnitude):</b> The Deviant automatically learns one of the target\u2019s relevant desires that can be used to satisfy this Scar.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Aware (\u20132 Magnitude):</b> Exclusive with Guided, the Remade automatically learns all the target\u2019s relevant desires that can be used to satisfy this Scar.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Compelled (+0 Magnitude):</b> Rather than the choice of target being wholly at the Storyteller\u2019s whim, it must be someone matching certain criteria, one who takes a certain action, or a combination of the two. For example, the Broken might be compelled to bring joy to children, perform a service for the first person to pay her fee, or grant the last wishes of the dying. Targets can include Conviction Touchstones and other enemies (but not cohort members, Loyalty Touchstones, or other close allies) as long as they meet the criteria. The Deviant\u2019s obligation to a target persists until a new viable target presents himself, with each satisfied desire of the current target replaced with a compulsion to satisfy another until a new target is acquired.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Costly (+1 Magnitude):</b> The price of failure to satisfy this Scar is higher \u2014 aggravated damage for Health, medium Instability for Stability, and three Willpower for Will. This Deviation is not available if the Remade\u2019s price is Power.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Multitudinous (+1 Magnitude):</b> Choose a second price of failing to satisfy this Scar (Health, Power, Stability, or Will). The Deviant suffers both.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Crushing (+2 Magnitude):</b> As Multitudinous and exclusive with it, but the transformed suffers three prices of failing to satisfy the Scar.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Unyielding (+1 Magnitude):</b> Continued failure to satisfy this Scar causes the Remade to wither away. Any damage, Instability, or Willpower lost to this Scar cannot be healed/replenished until the Broken successfully satisfies the Scar. If the price is Power, fulfilling her obligation does not allow the Deviant to activate the entangled Variation until the beginning of the <i>next</i> chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T09:51:56-07:00","id":1537499,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused about the Magnitude 1 involvement of the Bystander Deviation in Scapegoat and the Power cost of Noblesse Oblige.<br /> <br /> As a +0 Deviation, there's no way to get rid of Bystander by e.g. healing medium Instability, and the effects include something roughly analogous to the core Involuntary Scars' &quot;at this Magnitude, this Scar is Overt&quot; effect, but is the intention basically that, as a Controlled Scar, Scapegoat can gain the ability to be used outside the presence of a Loyalty Touchstone at any time by permanently taking the drawbacks of Bystander?<br /> <br /> Per the existing material on determining how every available Magnitude of a Discrete Variation that can have its Magnitude adjusted, I'm guessing the intention is that even if you only take the Scar at Magnitude 1 you're still supposed to determine what choices will be made for the Scar's higher Magnitudes when you develop the Scar. If the Magnitude of the Scar above 1 is temporary, does this mean an entangled Magnitude 1 Variation might change categories from Persistent to Controlled and back again?<br /> <br /> Also, presumably the Power option is also disallowed if the Scar is unentangled, but that then runs into the problem of developing the Scar at Magnitude 1 from major instability, theoretically needing to determine its full Magnitude when it's developed, and then reaching a situation where it's the only unentangled Scar you have when you acquire a medium Instability. (&quot;Just don't do that&quot; is one workaround, obviously, and if the comparison to Discrete Variation Magnitude is flawed then a lot of this goes away, but changing Scar types altogether does present a fiddly situation regardless.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T13:01:47-07:00","id":1537520,"title":"","content":"Hrm. It might be better to make Bystander the default (and allow Scar Resistance) and fold the Loyalty Touchstone option into the Cohort effect.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I follow you regarding Discrete Variations. If a Scar imposes a Secondary Scar based on its Magnitude and its Magnitude later increases, the Secondary Scar's Magnitude would also increase; the Secondary Scar wouldn't change (and I don't think it would break anything if the exact effect is slightly different each time it becomes temporarily worse). As well, Scapegoat stipulates that any Scar it imposes is Persistent, so activation type isn't an issue.<br /> <br /> The Power option makes Noblesse Oblige a Controlled Scar, and Controlled Scars can't be unentangled. Might be worth spelling that out, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T17:09:45-07:00","id":1537535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537520#post1537520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I follow you regarding Discrete Variations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Analogy for Noblesse Oblige; I split the second and third paragraphs up for readability without realizing it made that unclear, but what I was supposing was a possible reading where if you develop this Scar that potentially changes the activation method you would need to determine if it can do so at any point along its Magnitude (and when).<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, the Multitudinous and Crushing Deviations seem to underline how mechanically weird it is to have Power turn the Scar Controlled (the other prices come due despite Power ostensibly making the Scar a thing solely related to using entangled Variations). There's already Persistent Scars like Maintenance or the Alternate Persona Deviations that conditionally lock out entangled Variations from being used, but other than being Repeatable and therefore able to entangle more Variations by volume using a Scar of the same name, there doesn't seem to be any obvious reason why this should be a Controlled Scar constituting a price to be paid for activating Variations rather than a Persistent quality that can interfere with its entangled Variations. Does anything break if Power instead makes the Scar Toggled-Only like Maintenance or the Draining Deviation of Bane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T20:08:56-07:00","id":1537594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537535#post1537535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Analogy for Noblesse Oblige; I split the second and third paragraphs up for readability without realizing it made that unclear, but what I was supposing was a possible reading where if you develop this Scar that potentially changes the activation method you would need to determine if it can do so at any point along its Magnitude (and when).<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, the Multitudinous and Crushing Deviations seem to underline how mechanically weird it is to have Power turn the Scar Controlled (the other prices come due despite Power ostensibly making the Scar a thing solely related to using entangled Variations). There's already Persistent Scars like Maintenance or the Alternate Persona Deviations that conditionally lock out entangled Variations from being used, but other than being Repeatable and therefore able to entangle more Variations by volume using a Scar of the same name, there doesn't seem to be any obvious reason why this should be a Controlled Scar constituting a price to be paid for activating Variations rather than a Persistent quality that can interfere with its entangled Variations. Does anything break if Power instead makes the Scar Toggled-Only like Maintenance or the Draining Deviation of Bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the feedback. Let me tinker with this a bit and get back to you in a couple of days, as I'm too tired to do so just now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T04:03:59-07:00","id":1537607,"title":"","content":"Chapter Six is about character arcs, whether they're victories in spite of seemingly insurmountable odds, poignant tragedies, or something else entirely. Today we preview some mechanical guidance around End Stage. A section about the broad arc of chronicles is available for free at the link in my signature (with the full text of the chapter available to patrons).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Supernova</span></b><br /> <br /> As described in Chapter Three (p. XX), Variations have intentional limits to their range, duration, and scale. A Deviant in End Stage, however, can often break those boundaries. Most of the time, End Stage merely supercharges one aspect of each of the Broken\u2019s Magnitude 5 Variations until the end of the chapter. This can still have a considerable impact:<br /> <br /> <b>Control:</b> Scar Finesse rolls to activate or target the Variation enjoy a +3 bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlarged Area:</b> The Variation affects a larger area than usual. If it is not Directed, it grants its benefits to all allies, all non-enemies, or all logical targets within 10 yards/meters. If it is an Aura, its radius extends twice Scar Power times farther than usual (doubled at 1 Scar Power, quadrupled at 2 Scar Power, etc.). If it is Directed, the Deviant may affect multiple targets per turn (no greater than Scar Finesse) and any number of targets may fall under its sway at a time (rather than being limited by Scar Power); resolve multiple targeting as a long burst (<b>Deviant</b>, p. 198). Alternatively, a Directed effect\u2019s range is increased by a factor of 10.<br /> <br /> <b>Greater Duration:</b> Once activated, the Variation lasts until the end of the chapter instead of until the end of the scene. If the Variation has the Perpetual keyword, once activated, it counts as being Persistent and Perpetual even if ordinarily Controlled or Involuntary.<br /> <br /> <b>Instinctive:</b> The Remade may activate or deactivate the Variation reflexively. If Directed, the Broken can direct its effects as a reflexive action once for each of her turns. She can do this at a time other than her own turn, but once she directs the Variation reflexively, she may not do so again until the beginning of her next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Limitless:</b> Variation effects that are limited to once per scene, chapter, or story do not have this limit.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifted Scars:</b> The Scar entangled with the Variation changes. This could be a difference within the same Scar (which things trigger his Phobia, for example, or what behavior Subliminal Conditioning compels), or it could be a complete change in the Scar.<br /> <br /> <b>Super-Potent:</b> The Variation gains capabilities normally impossible for it (see below).<br /> <br /> <b>Synergy:</b> The Variation\u2019s effects bleed into one or more of the Broken\u2019s other Variations.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Super-Potent Examples</b></span><br /> <br /> The below are examples of what a Variation might be capable of if made super-potent or if synergizing with similar Variations. Each lists several examples of Variations appropriate to the effect, but this is by no means an exhaustive list.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Awareness:</b> The Broken\u2019s senses penetrate phenomena relevant to the Variation with perfect clarity. She enjoys a two-die bonus to Wits rolls. She may also ask the Storyteller questions about anything in the Variation\u2019s purview that she can perceive and receive accurate answers, although the Storyteller may call for Scar Finesse rolls for unusually subtle phenomena. <i>Predator\u2019s Cunning, Precognition, Sensor Array, Specialized Sense</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Disaster:</b> The Deviant may create a level 4 Extreme Environment relevant to the Variation. He is immune to this environment\u2019s effects and any Environmental Tilts it causes. <i>Bioluminescence, Electrokinesis, Environmental Adaptation, Pyrokinesis, Storm-Caller</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Gargantuan:</b> The Remade can take the shape of larger objects or creatures, increasing maximum Size by 10. <i>Animal Transformation, Gigantic, Matter Transformation</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Ghost:</b> The Deviant is undetectable and can pass through any substance at her normal Speed. <i>Boneless, Camouflage, Miniaturization, Out of Phase</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Kill:</b> Whether by means of a powerful Lash or telepathic power that causes victims to die of fright, the Deviant\u2019s Variations become honed for killing. Each turn, as a reflexive action, the Remade may make a Scar Finesse roll. Each success takes a Baseline in range out of the fight. <i>Creeping Dread, Lash, Superhuman Strength, Telekinesis</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Mark:</b> The Remade inflicts permanent damage on the target, imposing a Magnitude 3 Scar appropriate to the Variation (Magnitude 5, if the roll to target the Variation is an exceptional success). This is permanent for most Baselines; others can overcome it by devoting a story to recovering from the damage in some way. <i>Cryokinesis, Fate\u2019s Agent, Lash, Memory Thief, Telepathy</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Narration:</b> The Broken may introduce a convenient fact or plot twist to the scene that is relevant to the Variation. The Storyteller may veto any unreasonable suggestions but is encouraged to permit most scenarios. The first time the Deviant does this in a scene, the effect is automatic. Additional uses require successful Scar Finesse rolls with a cumulative \u20131 penalty, and once the Remade fails one of these rolls, she cannot attempt further plot twists in the current scene. <i>Hidden Compartments, Pheromones, Superhuman Presence, Superhuman Wits</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Perfection:</b> The Deviant acts with perfect grace or thinks with perfect clarity. Choose Mental, Physical, or Social, as appropriate to the Variation. All the Remade\u2019s actions of that type enjoy the rote quality, and she is treated as having three dots in each Skill of that type in which she has fewer than three dots. <i>Blessing, Hyper-Competence, Omnicompetence, Superhuman Attribute</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Portal:</b> The Broken can open a gateway large enough for two people to walk through at a time, which remains open for a few minutes (a few turns, in action scenes). Its destination reflects the Variation used to create it. Translocation might lead to any location in the world that she has ever been, for example, Astral Travel to one of her sleeping Touchstones, and Otherworldly Connection to a random location in the otherworld connected to her. <i>Astral Travel, Otherworldly Connection, Shadows of the Past, Translocation</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Travel:</b> The Deviant is capable of incredible speeds by air, land, or water (as appropriate), doubling the normal Speed of these forms of travel. She may also dodge without using her next action and does not lose her Defense when targeted by firearms and other attacks that ignore Defense. <i>Aquatic, Enhanced Speed, Flight</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Unkillable:</b> The Broken is functionally invulnerable to physical harm, shrugging off damage and Tilts that reflect injury (although not ones that represent fetters or environmental factors). <i>Anomalous Biology, Carapace, Rapid Healing, Superhuman Stamina</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Extinction Burst</b></span><br /> <br /> As the dramatic conclusion to End Stage draws near, the Deviant\u2019s soul disintegrates under the intensity of her Variations. Most Remade in End Stage never experience this. It is a final surrender to the Divergence from which there is no coming back. Sometimes, the extinction burst reflects the Broken\u2019s state of mind or goal at the time she entered End Stage, but oftentimes it is not so organized, simply a lashing out at random.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems:</b> When a Remade has the End Stage Condition, their player may elect to experience an extinction burst. Instead of dying at the end of the current chapter, the character dies at the end of the current <i>scene</i>. Even the catharsis of destroying a Conviction Touchstone cannot reverse End Stage once it reaches this point. Choose one of the following, or suggest a new one with Storyteller permission:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Anomaly:</b> The Deviant becomes the center point of an anomaly. The area and everyone in it might be caught in a time loop, for example, or everyone is frozen in place as the Remade\u2019s telepathic control arrests their control over their muscles. The exact radius and duration of this effect is up to the Storyteller, but it typically affects no less than a city block and ends no sooner than the end of the current chapter.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Crystalize:</b> The Broken\u2019s powers manifest as an object, likely one of occult power. Troupes with access to <b>The Clades Companion</b> may build this as a prototype.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Divergence Event:</b> The Deviant\u2019s soul sends out an occult shriek that cracks the souls of all nearby Baselines. Most die or suffer Scars with no Variations, but some Diverge. The exact radius of this event is up to the Storyteller, but it shouldn\u2019t be less than a city block.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Explosion:</b> The power within the Broken explodes out of him with enough force to topple buildings. Baselines at ground zero are killed instantly. The exact radius of this explosion is up to the Storyteller, but it shouldn\u2019t be less than a city block.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Miracle:</b> Instead of exploding in a wash of terrifying or destructive force, the Deviant\u2019s soul flows out in restorative ways. It might reverse the last few minutes, undoing the damage done by an accident or natural disaster, for example, or restore all the dead in the area to life. The exact radius and limits of this are up to the Storyteller, but it shouldn\u2019t be less than a city block.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Occult Scar:</b> The disintegration of the Remade\u2019s soul leaves a permanent mark on the area. It might become haunted, for example, or gravity might not work as expected. The exact radius of this is up to the Storyteller, but it shouldn\u2019t be less than the size of a small building and could encompass an area measured in city blocks \u2014 or even miles, in rare cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T04:02:24-07:00","id":1537681,"title":"","content":"Today's preview of <i>Shallow Graves</i> comes from Chapter Seven, which explores the formation and dynamics of cohorts. Among the tricks a cohort often has up its sleeve are Techniques, which are &quot;off-label&quot; uses for their Variations. While these can enhance an individual Deviant by granting an equipment bonus or impeding an opponent, they are often used to support or protect other members of the cohort in some way. Below are the basic systems for Techniques, as well as a few of examples from the book.<br /> <br /> Access to the appendices is available for free at the link in my signature (with the full text of Shallow Graves accessible to patrons).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Techniques</span><br /> <br /> Humans are a creative lot. Give them a problem, and they will quickly seek out tools in their environment that might solve it. They\u2019ll wield a tool one way, and then another, and then attack the problem with it from a completely different direction until the problem is solved. A tool or technique that serves them faithfully once often finds itself applied to new problems \u2014 sometimes in ways for which the tool is not ideal. \u201cWhen all you have is a hammer, everything looks like a nail,\u201d as the old saying goes.<br /> <br /> The Remade are no exception. Once they overcome the initial shock of the Divergence, Deviants experiment with their newfound abilities \u2014 whether in a systematic way or only in moments of desperation \u2014 and discover ways to use them. The obvious applications (the ones printed in <b>Deviant</b> and its supplements) come naturally, of course, but trial and error yield unobvious ones, too. These crude tools occasionally prove worthless, but enough of these approaches to problem-solving through Variations succeed to encourage the transformed to apply them to new problems.<br /> <br /> Over time, if they live long enough, Broken develop favored alternate uses for their abilities. Such applications cease being ad hoc improvisations and develop into formal techniques. Most never pass beyond the transformed who developed them. After all, even the cleverest use of telekinetic powers is useless to anyone who doesn\u2019t possess telekinesis (which is nearly everyone). But some have principles that can be applied to other Variations \u2014 and some Remade meet others who share their abilities \u2014 which allows one Deviant to teach their techniques to another. Remade who teach their techniques (or who help other Deviants develop techniques appropriate to their own Variations) are quite common among the Devoted, but a few such mentors exist among Renegades.<br /> <br /> In <b>Deviant: The Renegades</b>, these novel applications of the Broken\u2019s Variations are represented by <b>Techniques</b>. <b>Technique Basics</b><br /> <br /> <br /> No Variation permits the use of every Technique. The player must supply a narrative justification for why a Variation (or Adaptation or Form) allows a given Technique, which must be one the Storyteller finds reasonable. This will usually reflect the Variation\u2019s mechanics as-written, but in some cases the specific manifestation of that Variation for a Deviant can serve as a rationale. Even if a Variation generally justifies a Technique, it will not work in every situation. A quill plucked from the Remade\u2019s Deadly Ichor might work as a crude lockpick, but it will be useless against a magnetic keycard reader.<br /> <br /> To use a Technique, the Variation must be active first.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Learning Techniques</span><br /> <br /> \u2022 Although Remade benefit from practicing a Technique until they have mastered it, any Deviant with an appropriate Variation can improvise a given Technique. A Deviant can improvise a Technique once per chapter. Adaptations can reset this limit.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Whenever the Remade increases his Acclimation, he learns one new Technique for free. He may choose this immediately or save it for a time when he needs it, purchasing it mid-scene, if needed.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Broken may master additional Techniques by purchasing the Mastered Technique Merit (p. XX).<br /> <br /> \u2022 Whether gained by raising Acclimation or buying a Merit, a purchased (<b>Mastered</b>) Technique is more potent than an improvised one. However, although many Variations can express the same Technique, when purchasing a Technique, the Deviant must decide which Variation she uses to accomplish it. She must further specify its exact effects. For example, a purchased Technique based on the improvised effect of giving the Remade an equipment bonus on Skill checks must specify not just the Skills it enhances (typically one or two such Skills) but the specific applications of the Skills that benefit. It\u2019s as narrow as a Specialty \u2014 useful when it applies but by no means applying to all situations involving its Skill.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Technique Effects</span><br /> <br /> Most Techniques provide one of the following benefits:<br /> <br /> \u2022 If using a Variation to perform a mundane action, either replace the normal Attribute + Skill roll with a Scar Finesse roll or treat the Variation as equipment with a bonus equal to the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude \u2014 chosen when invoking the Technique. This equipment lasts until the end of the scene and does not stack with the Variation\u2019s normal bonus to rolls/resistance. <b>Mastered:</b> The Scar Finesse roll enjoys a +2 bonus, or the equipment bonus is instead the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If improving a static trait (like Defense, Speed, or armor), increase the trait by the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude. This improvement requires an action and lasts until the beginning of your next turn. <b>Mastered:</b> This is instead the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If using a Variation to set up or aid an ally in the scene, add dice equal to the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude to the ally\u2019s roll, or make a Scar Finesse roll and add your successes as dice to their roll (as a teamwork action) \u2014 chosen when invoking the Technique. This affects a single roll. <b>Mastered:</b> The Scar Finesse roll enjoys a +2 bonus, or the bonus is instead the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If using a Variation to create a melee weapon, it has a damage bonus equal to half the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude (rounded up), minus 1. The weapon is improvised and suffers a \u20131 penalty to attacks. Producing the weapon requires an action, but it lasts until the end of the scene. <b>Mastered:</b> The weapon does not suffer a penalty to attacks, and the damage bonus is instead half the greater of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude (rounded up), minus 1.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If imposing a penalty to an unwilling character\u2019s mundane action, it requires a Scar Finesse roll as though it were a Directed effect, the penalty it imposes is equal to the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude, and it lasts for a single roll. This requires the Deviant\u2019s action for the turn and does not stack with the Variation\u2019s normal penalty to rolls/resistance. <b>Mastered:</b> This penalty is instead the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude.<br /> <br /> \u2022 If worsening another person\u2019s static trait (like Defense, Speed, or armor), it requires a Scar Finesse roll as though it were a Directed effect. If successful, reduce the trait by the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude. This requires an action and lasts until the beginning of your next turn. <b>Mastered:</b> The reduction is instead the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude.<br /> <br /> \u2022 A Variation can grant an ally a Magnitude 1 Variation for a turn and without requiring the ally to use an action to activate it. This must be one the Variation could potentially impart. Using Holographic Projection to hide an ally (Camouflage) makes sense but using it to impart Aquatic does not. <b>Mastered:</b> The temporary Variation can be up to Magnitude 2.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Example Techniques</span><br /> <br /> The following are examples of Techniques Deviants are likely to have. Each lists likely Variations that could be used to produce the effect, but these are by no means exhaustive. Each also provides the effect of mastering it, rather than improvising it. Some follow the guidelines above, while others use mechanics unique to them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Bodyguard</span><br /> <br /> <b>Sample Variations:</b> Carapace, Extra Appendages, Predator\u2019s Cunning, Precognition<br /> <br /> As an action, the Remade blocks, deflects, or otherwise turns aside attacks on the ally against which the bodyguard would enjoy her Defense. This can also represent Variations that allow the bodyguard to give the ally advance warning of danger or to move him out of harm\u2019s way. This increases the ally\u2019s Defense by the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude until the Broken\u2019s next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastered:</b> Use the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude, instead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Clear Threat</span><br /> <br /> <b>Sample Variations:</b> Gigantic, Lash, Matter Emulation, Shadow Selves<br /> <br /> By making himself an obvious threat, the Remade draws enemy fire to himself, potentially sparing less battle-ready members of his cohort. As a reflexive action after taking an opponent out of the fight in a turn, make a Scar Finesse roll. If successful, a number of Baselines in the scene equal to the lower of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude \u2014 or a single non-Baseline opponent \u2014 concentrate their attacks on the Broken next turn. They remain focused on him until he is no longer a threat or until he fails to take one of their number out of the fight on his turn.<br /> <br /> This effect is cumulative with successive turns. As long as the Deviant continues eliminating opponents each turn, he attracts the attention of more and more of the remaining enemies.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastered:</b> Use the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude, instead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Decoy</span><br /> <br /> <b>Sample Variations:</b> Beast Mastery, Bioluminescence, Pyrokinesis, Storm-Caller<br /> <br /> The Deviant uses Variations to attract attention to herself. If she remains in the scene, allies enjoy a bonus equal to the lower of her Scar Power or Variation Magnitude to their Stealth rolls and other actions to operate unnoticed for as long as the distraction lasts.<br /> <br /> She may instead provoke enemies into giving chase. For each success she achieves on a Scar Finesse roll, she draws away four Baseline (or one non-Baseline) pursuers. This can be resolved following normal chase rules (<b>Deviant</b>, p. XX), with the pursuit ending either when the Remade gives the hunters the slip or they catch up with her. Each turn of a chase is 30 seconds to one minute, which can give allies a clear window to overcome the remaining guards, plant the explosives, or otherwise exploit their numeric advantage.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastered:</b> If remaining in the scene, use the <i>higher</i> of Scar Power or Variation Magnitude, instead. If fleeing, each success draws away twice as many people.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T04:18:11-07:00","id":1537682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537535#post1537535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Analogy for Noblesse Oblige; I split the second and third paragraphs up for readability without realizing it made that unclear, but what I was supposing was a possible reading where if you develop this Scar that potentially changes the activation method you would need to determine if it can do so at any point along its Magnitude (and when).<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, the Multitudinous and Crushing Deviations seem to underline how mechanically weird it is to have Power turn the Scar Controlled (the other prices come due despite Power ostensibly making the Scar a thing solely related to using entangled Variations). There's already Persistent Scars like Maintenance or the Alternate Persona Deviations that conditionally lock out entangled Variations from being used, but other than being Repeatable and therefore able to entangle more Variations by volume using a Scar of the same name, there doesn't seem to be any obvious reason why this should be a Controlled Scar constituting a price to be paid for activating Variations rather than a Persistent quality that can interfere with its entangled Variations. Does anything break if Power instead makes the Scar Toggled-Only like Maintenance or the Draining Deviation of Bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>Coming back at this after getting more sleep, the simple solution (which you suggested) is to simply say &quot;your Variation doesn't work until you fulfill the condition, and it is suppressed if it is a Perpetual Variation.&quot; I also seem to have missed an opportunity to have a +2 effect that shuts off <i>all</i> your Variations until you satisfy the condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T04:37:16-07:00","id":1537685,"title":"","content":"How much would you rate a Merit that lets the Broken improvise a Technique on a successful Scar Finesse roll, instead of getting one per chapter?<br /> <br /> As well, I'd like to see a Technique Effect the essentially lets you emulate an entire Variation, so long as it's consistent with your character concept: this would normally take the form of pointing to a Variation on your character sheet as justification; but I could also see using a Form or even an Adaptation to justify the emulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:18:32-07:00","id":1537689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537685#post1537685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much would you rate a Merit that lets the Broken improvise a Technique on a successful Scar Finesse roll, instead of getting one per chapter?<br /> <br /> As well, I'd like to see a Technique Effect the essentially lets you emulate an entire Variation, so long as it's consistent with your character concept: this would normally take the form of pointing to a Variation on your character sheet as justification; but I could also see using a Form or even an Adaptation to justify the emulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hesitant to remove the per-chapter limit (other than by resetting it with an Adaptation) because it opens up so much flexibility even <i>with</i> that limit. The Practical Adaptation originally did something like that but seemed too likely to be disruptive if turned loose on the wrong group. In one that feels comfortable with that, though, you could probably use the Scar Finesse roll requirement <i>instead</i> of the per-chapter limit or come up with a custom Merit with an Acclimation requirement that reflects it for just one character.<br /> <br /> Body Modification and Matter Emulation provide starting points for a Variation with that kind of flexibility. Perhaps an inexpensive (2-ish dots, Acclimation 1) Merit that &quot;ties&quot; ME to one of your Variations instead of to a particular substance would get you what you're looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:19:03-07:00","id":1537690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537685#post1537685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much would you rate a Merit that lets the Broken improvise a Technique on a successful Scar Finesse roll, instead of getting one per chapter?<br /> <br /> As well, I'd like to see a Technique Effect the essentially lets you emulate an entire Variation, so long as it's consistent with your character concept: this would normally take the form of pointing to a Variation on your character sheet as justification; but I could also see using a Form or even an Adaptation to justify the emulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you could have a technique where you can emulate another variation at rank 1 in very specific circumstances. Mastery would allow you to emulate it at rank 2. For example, you could use Holographic Projection 3 to replicate Bioluminescence 1 in situations where there is no other strong light source. Or maybe you can use Absorb Instability to emulate Healer on anyone you have used the former on in the same story. Could also require that the Variation have a magnitude minimum of 3 or higher to show that this Technique is particularly potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:27:24-07:00","id":1537692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537690#post1537690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe you could have a technique where you can emulate another variation at rank 1 in very specific circumstances. Mastery would allow you to emulate it at rank 2. For example, you could use Holographic Projection 3 to replicate Bioluminescence 1 in situations where there is no other strong light source. Or maybe you can use Absorb Instability to emulate Healer on anyone you have used the former on in the same story. Could also require that the Variation have a magnitude minimum of 3 or higher to show that this Technique is particularly potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that would also be reasonable, especially with the Mag 3 minimum. The &quot;give an ally a Variation for a turn&quot; effect is so limited only because &quot;give yourself any low-Mag Variation you want&quot; is kind of the Mutants' shtick, and I didn't want to diminish their signature Adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:35:59-07:00","id":1537694,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Having a particular Variation as basically a low-mag setting for another Variation seemed like it wouldn't step on the toes of Mutants. Either way the Techniques really allow for that creativity at the table while giving players even more ways to personalize their characters. Excellent work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:53:54-07:00","id":1537696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537694#post1537694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Having a particular Variation as basically a low-mag setting for another Variation seemed like it wouldn't step on the toes of Mutants. Either way the Techniques really allow for that creativity at the table while giving players even more ways to personalize their characters. Excellent work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'm really pleased with the way they've turned out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T07:28:15-07:00","id":1537703,"title":"","content":"I had been thinking of making the \u201croll Scar Finesse instead of getting one per chapter\u201d thing as a Merit, because I'm well aware of how powerful that can be. But I rather like the idea of maybe making it a Deviation for Body Modification and/or Matter Emulation instead, or even as a Standard Deviation: with this Deviation, you can use the Variation to emulate another variation on a successful Scar Finesse roll. (The Storyteller is free to apply this Deviation to any other Variation where he thinks it's suitable; but that's strictly at his discretion.)<br /> <br /> But instead of limiting it to Magnitude 1 or 2, maybe the emulated Variation can be of any Magnitude; but you must entangle it with a secondary Controlled Scar of its own? Let's say, for instance, that Matter Emulation doesn't let me turn into a liquid and flow through a pipe or between iron bars; I'd emulate that using Out of Phase 3 (Body) or Out of Phase 4; but that's not possible if I'm restricted to Magnitude 1 or 2. So instead, I go ahead and emulate the Magnitude 3 or 4 Variation, but use a Controlled Scar of sufficient Magnitude to do so. <br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026 As a +1 Deviation, the improvised Variation needs to be entangled with a Controlled Scar with more Magnitude than it has; as a +2 Deviation, it can be entangled with a Scar of equal Magnitude. And this is on top of whatever Scars are entangled with the Variation you're using to do the emulating. Or something like that. <br /> <br /> Frankly, I'd much prefer an \u201cany Magnitude is available; but it must be entangled with a sufficiently severe Controlled Scar\u201d approach to \u201cyou get it at Magnitude 1 or 2\u201d when dealing with improvised Variations: sometimes the effect that you're trying to produce simply isn't something that a Magnitude 1 Variation can represent. For instance, I don't know if it's possible to use Matter Emulation as written to liquify your body enough to squeeze through an iron-mesh filter; but if it isn't, I'd want to be able to use this Deviation in order to emulate Out of Phase (Body), which is Magnitude 3, or even Out of Phase with Magnitude 4. The former <i>might </i>be doable by applying a Standard Deviation to reduce its effective Magnitude to 2 (such as something that prevents you from passing through watertight barriers); but that becomes a major hassle and an unnecessary complication which potentially prevents me from doing something that makes perfect sense within the in-game setting; so I'd rather just call it a case of emulating a Magnitude 3 Variation and requiring the Broken character to use a Magnitude 4 Scar to activate it. <br /> <br /> And this should apply to granting an ally a temporary use of a Variation, too: the person using the Technique decides on a suitable Variation to grant, which can be of any Magnitude; it just needs to be conceptually consistent with the Variation that he's using to do the emulation. But he has to use a Controlled Scar of greater Magnitude than the granted Variation in order to do it, though Mastery lets him do it with a Controlled Scar equal to the Magnitude of the granted Variation. <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T07:50:54-07:00","id":1537705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537703#post1537703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say, for instance, that Matter Emulation doesn't let me turn into a liquid and flow through a pipe or between iron bars; I'd emulate that using Out of Phase 3 (Body) or Out of Phase 4[\u2026]<br /> <br /> For instance, I don't know if it's possible to use Matter Emulation as written to liquify your body enough to squeeze through an iron-mesh filter; but if it isn't, I'd want to be able to use this Deviation in order to emulate Out of Phase (Body), which is Magnitude 3, or even Out of Phase with Magnitude 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would just like to point out that Boneless 3 is the corebook Variation to use for turning into a liquid to get through grilles and grates or move through pipes; you don't need to fiddle around with intangibility to produce the effect of &quot;I am capable of liquidlike flexibility.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T16:55:28-07:00","id":1537805,"title":"","content":"Looks like we lost a few posts during that forum outage. Dataweaver said something about possibly tying Techniques and Static rules such that Static can be used to make Techniques more effective. I'd like to unpack that a bit. What kind of advantage did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> BTW, I put up some of the interior art from <i>Shallow Graves</i> at the link in my signature this morning, if folks are interested in seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T18:26:31-07:00","id":1537807,"title":"","content":"Maybe something as simple as being able to spend a point of Static to treat a Technique to get the Mastered effect even if it isn't Mastered, but only when you're using the Technique to help a teammate or Loyalty anchor, or to interfere with a Conviction Anchor. Or maybe invest a point of Static in the Technique to treat it as Mastered in all ways, so long as the subject is one of the above. I'd want to playtest to make sure it doesn't break the game; but I think it could work.<br /> <br /> Or maybe both: invest a point of Static in a Technique to let you use it as often as you want, as long as the subject is one of those that you're closely connected to; and spend a point of Static to get the Mastered effect instead of the standard effect, but only if the subject is one of those that you're closely connected to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Elaborated a bit, and fixed a typo. 06-27-2024, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T19:19:48-07:00","id":1537808,"title":"","content":"I've added it to my list to noodle with in errata. Speaking of errata, I've made some adjustments to Noblesse Oblige in response to comments here and elsewhere. Is it an improvement?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Noblesse Oblige (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\"><b>Keywords:</b> Mental, Social; Subtle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">The Broken suffers a supernatural compulsion to fulfill the desires of strangers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">At Magnitude \u2022, the Deviant\u2019s player may accept a Beat whenever she performs a random act of kindness for a stranger that results in a complication for her or her cohort.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">At Magnitude \u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022, and up to once per chapter the Storyteller may choose a character the Remade is compelled to help, which will not be a Conviction Touchstone. The Deviant must ensure that the target fulfills a Vice, Virtue, Aspiration, or esoteric drive (such as furthering a Touchstone). The Remade knows which person is her target but doesn\u2019t automatically receive knowledge of his desires; she needs to learn that information on her own. Unless the target accomplishes his goal before the end of the <i>next</i> chapter, the Deviant suffers one of the consequences below at the beginning of the following chapter, chosen at the time she develops this Scar:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Health:</b> The Remade suffers a point of lethal damage that cannot be healed by supernatural effects.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Power:</b> The Deviant cannot activate the entangled Variations until she fulfills the obligation. If it is Persistent and Perpetual, it ceases to function until then.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Stability:</b> The Broken suffers a minor Instability.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Will:</b> The Deviant loses a point of Willpower.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">If the Storyteller chooses a new target, it frees the Remade from any existing obligation (and potential consequences for failing to uphold it).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022, but the Broken has fewer avenues by which to satisfy her compulsion. Choose two of the following when the Deviant develops this Scar, and helping the target fulfill these no longer satisfies the conditions of this Scar: Esoteric, Short-Term Aspiration, Long-Term Aspiration, Vice, or Virtue.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">At Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022, but only one type of desire satisfies the conditions of this Scar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\"><b>Deviations</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">Except for Compelled, Kind, and Cruel, all the below Deviations are only allowed if the base effect is Magnitude \u2022\u2022 or higher.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Guided (\u20131 Magnitude):</b> The Deviant automatically learns one of the target\u2019s relevant desires that can be used to satisfy this Scar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Aware (\u20132 Magnitude):</b> Exclusive with Guided, the Remade automatically learns all the target\u2019s relevant desires that can be used to satisfy this Scar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Compelled (+0 Magnitude):</b> Rather than the choice of target being wholly at the Storyteller\u2019s whim, it must be someone matching certain criteria, one who takes a certain action, or a combination of the two. For example, the Broken might be compelled to bring joy to children, perform a service for the first person to pay her fee, or grant the last wishes of the dying. The Deviant\u2019s player decides when choosing this effect whether targets can <i>never</i> include Conviction Touchstones (or other enemies), Loyalty Touchstones, cohort members, or other close allies (even if they meet the criteria) OR whether it can include <i>any</i> of these as long as they meet the criteria. The Deviant\u2019s obligation to a target persists until a new viable target presents himself, with each satisfied desire of the current target replaced with a compulsion to satisfy another until a new target is acquired.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Kind (-1 Magnitude):</b> As Compelled and exclusive with it and Cruel, except targets <i>never</i> include Conviction Touchstones or other enemies, but they <i>can</i> include Loyalty Touchstones, cohort members, or close allies \u2014 as long as they meet the criteria.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Cruel (+1 Magnitude):</b> As Compelled and exclusive with it and Kind, except targets <i>never</i> include Loyalty Touchstones, cohort members, or close allies, but they <i>can</i> include Conviction Touchstones or other enemies \u2014 as long as they meet the criteria.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Costly (+1 Magnitude):</b> The price of failure to satisfy this Scar is higher \u2014 aggravated damage for Health, medium Instability for Stability, and three Willpower for Will. If the Remade\u2019s price is Power, it shuts down additional Variations equal to (6 \u2013 Scar Resistance)..</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Multitudinous (+1 Magnitude):</b> Choose a second price of failing to satisfy this Scar (Health, Power, Stability, or Will). The Deviant suffers both.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Crushing (+2 Magnitude):</b> As Multitudinous and exclusive with it, but the transformed suffers three prices of failing to satisfy the Scar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Unyielding (+1 Magnitude):</b> Continued failure to satisfy this Scar causes the Remade to wither away. Any damage, Instability, or Willpower lost to this Scar cannot be healed/replenished until the Broken successfully satisfies the Scar. If the price is Power, fulfilling her obligation does not allow the Deviant to activate the entangled Variation until the beginning of the <i>next</i> chapter.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T19:44:21-07:00","id":1537809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537808#post1537808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've added it to my list to noodle with in errata. Speaking of errata, I've made some adjustments to Noblesse Oblige in response to comments here and elsewhere. Is it an improvement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks solid enough unless I'm overlooking something.* Interesting to see that Compelled has been unfolded into further targeting options.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I didn't originally ask for clarification on this because I was more focused on changing Scar types, but is the intention with Compelled and its variants that the default Magnitude 2 &quot;the ST may call this in once per chapter&quot; effect is replaced by the character always having another character's desires to fulfill at the start of a chapter for the purposes of the Scar's consequences, replacing the target of the deviant's assistance as new ones are discovered, rather than potentially being able to go a chapter without being tapped to help someone?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* It's potentially a niche circumstance, but Costly with a cost of Power being potentially free Magnitude if all the deviant's Variations are entangled with Noblesse Oblige may warrant a caveat a la Thin Skin not letting you lose more Health boxes than you would need to be alive.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T20:11:30-07:00","id":1537810,"title":"","content":"I've made a minor edit to my working version to account for that corner case. As for Compelled, perhaps:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#00000a\">\u2022 <b>Compelled (+0 Magnitude):</b> Rather than the choice of target being wholly at the Storyteller\u2019s whim, it must be someone matching certain criteria, one who takes a certain action, or a combination of the two. For example, the Broken might be compelled to bring joy to children, perform a service for the first person to pay her fee, or grant the last wishes of the dying. The Deviant\u2019s player decides when choosing this effect whether targets can <i>never</i> include Conviction Touchstones (or other enemies), Loyalty Touchstones, cohort members, or other close allies (even if they meet the criteria) OR whether it can include <i>any</i> of these as long as they meet the criteria. The Deviant\u2019s obligation to a target persists until the Remade satisfies the target\u2019s desire or a new viable target presents himself. No more than one such favor can be compelled of the Broken per chapter, nor does changing targets delay the consequences of failing to uphold the obligation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I want the option to have a person who knows your True Name (or whatever) forcing you do their bidding chapter after chapter, but I don't want that control to be as direct as Subliminal Conditioning and I don't want a player to be able to delay the obligation indefinitely by finding new targets who meet the criteria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T01:25:11-07:00","id":1537812,"title":"","content":"Is it feasible to tie <i>Noblesse Oblige</i> to a secondary Scar that will punish the Remade for not following through? I feel it would offer many more ways this mechanic could be used for character generation. It would also streamline listed costs in Health, Power, Stability and Will, as they're all preexisting Scars already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T08:04:59-07:00","id":1537820,"title":"","content":"Just a wee update here, but...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Shallow Graves will be going up for sale on Storyteller's Vault this Monday, July 1st.</span><br /> <br /> This is an errata collection version. I'll have an errata form and gather input until July 15th. The final version will replace this version once I've applied the errata, updated the p. XXs, and completed the index.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T07:00:06-07:00","id":1537858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537807#post1537807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe something as simple as being able to spend a point of Static to treat a Technique to get the Mastered effect even if it isn't Mastered, but only when you're using the Technique to help a teammate or Loyalty anchor, or to interfere with a Conviction Anchor. Or maybe invest a point of Static in the Technique to treat it as Mastered in all ways, so long as the subject is one of the above. I'd want to playtest to make sure it doesn't break the game; but I think it could work.<br /> <br /> Or maybe both: invest a point of Static in a Technique to let you use it as often as you want, as long as the subject is one of those that you're closely connected to; and spend a point of Static to get the Mastered effect instead of the standard effect, but only if the subject is one of those that you're closely connected to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastered is quite potent, and adjudicating what is and isn't helping someone else could be tricky to write mechanics for. Perhaps an option to spend Static instead of using an Adaptation to reset the per-chapter limit on improvised Techniques? I've made a note to add Scar Finesse roll improvised Techniques to the Storyteller's Guide as an optional rule, since <i>Black Vans</i> already has oodles of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T07:14:53-07:00","id":1537859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1537812#post1537812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it feasible to tie <i>Noblesse Oblige</i> to a secondary Scar that will punish the Remade for not following through? I feel it would offer many more ways this mechanic could be used for character generation. It would also streamline listed costs in Health, Power, Stability and Will, as they're all preexisting Scars already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ordinarily, I'd be onboard with that. I love things that reduce word count and increase flexibility. But I think in this case it would be unwieldy to create an easy-to-adjudicate system for determining which Scars are and aren't appropriate for Noblesse Oblige. WP/damage/Instability costs are straight out of Controlled Scars, but most Controlled Scars don't exact so clear a price; Degeneration is probably doable, but how does Tabula Rasa translate as a punishment? Persistent Scars, for the most part, could work, and I think it's a reasonably easy exercise for a table that wants to make it so failure to live up to Noblesse Oblige imposes a Mag 3 Persistent Scar that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T04:04:24-07:00","id":1537938,"title":"","content":"Shallow Graves is now live on <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\">The Storyteller's Vault</a>