view as well ? i really want this one to succeed even more<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T22:45:07-07:00","id":1538070,"title":"","content":"Been circling on the Merits chapter for a minute now and am curious about something with regards to Learned Magnitude:<br /> <br /> Does the note about the Acclimation prerequisite for the four-dot version being one higher than the two-dot version just mean that Learned Magnitude 4 has an Acclimation prerequisite of 3, or is the &quot;choose a Variation with a Magnitude no greater than&quot; note for the two-dot version likewise modified such that your Acclimation has to be two dots higher than the Magnitude of the Variation benefiting from the four-dot version? (i.e. can Learned Magnitude's Acclimation limit be phrased as &quot;Learned Magnitude can only increase a Variation's Magnitude as high as your Acclimation rating&quot;?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T05:30:53-07:00","id":1538080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1538070#post1538070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been circling on the Merits chapter for a minute now and am curious about something with regards to Learned Magnitude:<br /> <br /> Does the note about the Acclimation prerequisite for the four-dot version being one higher than the two-dot version just mean that Learned Magnitude 4 has an Acclimation prerequisite of 3, or is the &quot;choose a Variation with a Magnitude no greater than&quot; note for the two-dot version likewise modified such that your Acclimation has to be two dots higher than the Magnitude of the Variation benefiting from the four-dot version? (i.e. can Learned Magnitude's Acclimation limit be phrased as &quot;Learned Magnitude can only increase a Variation's Magnitude as high as your Acclimation rating&quot;?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that that language would be simpler. Learned Magnitude and Eased Scar both have an unintended exploit that I'm fixing, so cleaning up the language while I'm at it would be a good thing. Could you errata it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T13:49:36-07:00","id":1538150,"title":"","content":"I'm going to take awhile to sit down and actually start reading my way through the substance, I normally do that slow, but one thing I always check is PDF bookmarks, both because they're very good and useful when arranged properly, and because they often don't get arranged properly (even in the Onyx Path &quot;official&quot; releases). So I've submitted an early chunk of &quot;errata&quot; just looking on the flow of which bookmarks might be in the wrong subcategories, or confusingly sorted, or just consist of the letter &quot;A.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T18:16:49-07:00","id":1538160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1538150#post1538150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to take awhile to sit down and actually start reading my way through the substance, I normally do that slow, but one thing I always check is PDF bookmarks, both because they're very good and useful when arranged properly, and because they often don't get arranged properly (even in the Onyx Path &quot;official&quot; releases). So I've submitted an early chunk of &quot;errata&quot; just looking on the flow of which bookmarks might be in the wrong subcategories, or confusingly sorted, or just consist of the letter &quot;A.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's appreciated. Graphic design and layout aren't my areas of expertise, so I'm poorly equipped to judge them beyond &quot;der, that looks kinda weird to me, maybe?&quot;, and half the time, my instincts are wrong even on <i>that</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T13:33:03-07:00","id":1538213,"title":"","content":"I've submitted two different errata for this already, but I'm curious: What's the intent for how the &quot;Connected&quot; effect of Evil Twin works as relates to the normal systems for having multiple conspiracies in play at the same time, given that the described rationales for reduced effectiveness in both cases in Playing With Multiple Conspiracies don't apply to a group whose stated goal is messing with the Remade? Is there something that makes using the Hunted Condition like a Monstrous Conspicuous Appearance does mechanically or narratively undesirable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T04:21:48-07:00","id":1538230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1538213#post1538213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've submitted two different errata for this already, but I'm curious: What's the intent for how the &quot;Connected&quot; effect of Evil Twin works as relates to the normal systems for having multiple conspiracies in play at the same time, given that the described rationales for reduced effectiveness in both cases in Playing With Multiple Conspiracies don't apply to a group whose stated goal is messing with the Remade? Is there something that makes using the Hunted Condition like a Monstrous Conspicuous Appearance does mechanically or narratively undesirable?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that I need to clarify that, as the pseudo-conspiracy is intended to largely work <i>backwards</i> from the usual multi-conspiracy situation. Instead of generating Effort that slowly advances its Projects, the You-Hating Club gets to direct it into a single conspiracy action. It doesn't really have long-term designs beyond that.<br /> <br /> Hunted usually represents just one person, so if you neutralize that person, the threat goes away. Even if the Condition refreshes itself because of a Scar, it should still feel like just one enemy out to get you at any given time. With Evil Twin, I wanted to give the impression that a whole-ass <i>conspiracy</i> is out there with the sole intent of making your life a living hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T09:04:28-07:00","id":1538302,"title":"","content":"Q: how does Anomalous Biology affect a homunculus? Do they, by default, require food, air, (etc) if they don't have it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T10:32:38-07:00","id":1538306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1538302#post1538302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: how does Anomalous Biology affect a homunculus? Do they, by default, require food, air, (etc) if they don't have it?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default a Homunculus has no Health, disappears if it takes any damage, has set dicepools for things inside and outside its areas of expertise, has a limited understanding of the world around it and no volition of its own, and has its presence work like a Toggled Variation, meaning it doesn't last long enough to worry about food or sleep, doesn't have the luxury of unconsciousness or bleeding out or wound penalties or being poisoned, and doesn't have much of a mind to read. Many of the possible skins for a homunculus are things that don't need to worry about breathing or exposure, particularly given that even if it's &quot;killed&quot; you can summon it again next chapter with the same qualities.<br /> <br /> You could certainly construct a homunculus for which Anomalous Biology's various low-level passive effects are relevant, but the default systems are very much set up such that a homunculus is a fantastical channel for some or all of your Variations rather than a living creature that needs to breathe and eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T03:53:30-07:00","id":1538470,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder that the last day for errata feedback is Monday (7/15). <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScDqIhQ9k68HZT33re6sOw7jB_0fCoqvS6z50Z4eh7jTWXmGQ/viewform?usp=sf_link\" target=\"_blank\">You can access the errata form here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T05:51:21-07:00","id":1538731,"title":"","content":"Finally had time to purchase this book. Looking forward to soaking it all up during a long flight I have. One quick question, is there any reason why a player couldn't take on a Form after character creation. I only ask because the new Advanced Forms system does work off Merit dots. I was thinking about how a character, like Jean Grey, could work who starts out clearly a Cephalist, but eventually takes on Coactive traits through the Phoenix Force. Could easily be both Transitional and Symbiote Forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T05:59:37-07:00","id":1538733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1538731#post1538731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally had time to purchase this book. Looking forward to soaking it all up during a long flight I have. One quick question, is there any reason why a player couldn't take on a Form after character creation. I only ask because the new Advanced Forms system does work off Merit dots. I was thinking about how a character, like Jean Grey, could work who starts out clearly a Cephalist, but eventually takes on Coactive traits through the Phoenix Force. Could easily be both Transitional and Symbiote Forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no problem with doing so. Forms are kind of like self-contained character histories. If the narrative supports the addition of a new Form, I'd say go for it! The Jean Grey example is a good one, but you also have characters who, for example, suffer a horrible accident and end up having parts of themselves replaced with cybernetics. Or who make friends with some occult being they can summon for aid. Or who come into contact with an alien symbiote that hijacks their body and messes with their mind (lookin' at you, Spider Man/Venom). By the same token, it's reasonable to <i>lose</i> a Form due to narrative events, with the usual Sanctity of Merits refund.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T06:07:56-07:00","id":1538735,"title":"","content":"Perfect. And yes, Spider Man/Venom came to mind along with characters like Cable and Archangel. Seemed like a perfect mechanic to cover those tropes. Might homebrew a Condition or system that allows players to make these shifts when it narratively makes sense and how they would pay for it (i.e., losing Attributes or Merits to cover the Form cost). I can't say enough how much I wish Deviants was its own fully supported gameline. The work you are doinng on this game is astounding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:37:02-07:00","id":1538747,"title":"","content":"It <i>is</i> its own fully supported gameline. The only catch is that Paradox pulled the plug on the Chronicles of Darkness official releases, meaning that <b>Shallow Graves</b> and <b>Black Vans</b> need to use Storyteller's Vault to do an end-run around that. <br /> <br /> With that said: once <b>Black Vans</b> is out, what further support do you think the gameline needs? You've got the core book; the Devoted companion that lets you play on the side of the Conspiracies; the Clade Companion that supplements the core book with Forms, animals, gear, and Ephemeral Entities rules; the Player's Guide (Shallow Graves) which massively expands the player options; and the upcoming Storyteller's Guide (Black Vans) which will likewise massively expand the Storyteller's options. That's comparable to what the first edition of <b>Promethean</b> got. <br /> <br /> A possible answer to that would be \u201cworked examples\u201d. <b>Deviant</b> is a wonderful toolkit that lets you make whatever you want; but by the same token, that requires you to put in the work to create everything. Perhaps we could do with a series of Conspiracy books, each focusing on a sample Conspiracy and the Deviants that it produces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:41:53-07:00","id":1538755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1538747#post1538747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>is</i> its own fully supported gameline. The only catch is that Paradox pulled the plug on the Chronicles of Darkness official releases, meaning that <b>Shallow Graves</b> and <b>Black Vans</b> need to use Storyteller's Vault to do an end-run around that.<br /> <br /> With that said: once <b>Black Vans</b> is out, what further support do you think the gameline needs? You've got the core book; the Devoted companion that lets you play on the side of the Conspiracies; the Clade Companion that supplements the core book with Forms, animals, gear, and Ephemeral Entities rules; the Player's Guide (Shallow Graves) which massively expands the player options; and the upcoming Storyteller's Guide (Black Vans) which will likewise massively expand the Storyteller's options. That's comparable to what the first edition of <b>Promethean</b> got.<br /> <br /> A possible answer to that would be \u201cworked examples\u201d. <b>Deviant</b> is a wonderful toolkit that lets you make whatever you want; but by the same token, that requires you to put in the work to create everything. Perhaps we could do with a series of Conspiracy books, each focusing on a sample Conspiracy and the Deviants that it produces.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I think my point was more to share how unique and special this particular gameline is. A Night Horrors book would be great (and I know it's been hinted at) as would example Conspiracy books with RMCs and example campaigns would go a long way in making DtR more accessible. Maybe even different conspiracies at different threat levels to help players and STs understand more of how that should feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T12:35:02-07:00","id":1538776,"title":"","content":"A Night Horrors book is on my list. It's far enough out that I don't even have an outline for it, but my initial conception involves a <i>lot</i> of conspiracy write-ups (from Standing 1 to 10, although it will be weighted towards Standing 1-6 conspiracies) with Icons, STCs, Nodes, and interconnections between them - most of which can be easily transported piecemeal into an existing chronicle. Basically, it would be, if not an entire Web of Pain, at least a starting point for building an entire Web of Pain.<br /> <br /> Just as oodles of Variations and Scars serve as examples that make it easier to design new Variations and Scars, I think having oodles of conspiracies, Nodes, Icons, and Devoted will go a long way to making it easy to design new conspiracies (and their parts). My only concern with this approach is that I might end up shortchanging Ferals and rival Renegades in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T13:10:32-07:00","id":1538779,"title":"","content":"Any possibility of Ready Made Characters to come after Night Horrors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T13:17:59-07:00","id":1538780,"title":"","content":"In truth, that's not currently on my radar. I could probably work up some kind of jumpstart and/or RMC book, especially if there seems to be an appetite for it. But quite honestly, a big part of the appeal of the game for a lot of people is coming up with interesting character concepts, so I'm not sure how to build excitement around such a book. Maybe I'm way off-base and people would be thrilled to have a few one-shot-able scenarios (with pre-gens) that they can use to show off the game to players as a lure to something more long-term. Even a NH book is at least half a year away from serious production, so we're looking at a minimum year beyond that before I can start pulling together some shorter projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T13:38:38-07:00","id":1538784,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. I was thinking it would be useful to see some of the Advanced Forms on display along with some other characters who could be picked up and played with. In a dream world, DtR could have a character tropes book where example write ups are done for some common tropes that people might choose or draw inspiration from. Something like how Aberrant has a list of character templates at the back of the core book. I always found those sections useful for new players in games like Aberrant or Mutants &amp; Masterminds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T04:01:08-08:00","id":1545848,"title":"","content":"The post-errata version of <b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\">Shallow Graves</a></b> is now live on Storyteller's Vault.<br /> <br /> I'm currently working on the 2nd draft of <b>Black Vans</b>, which is a Deviant Storyteller's Guide I expect to release in 2025. Regular news updates and excerpts of the WIP are available at the bottom link of in signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T13:28:48-08:00","id":1545872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1545848#post1545848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The post-errata version of <b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\">Shallow Graves</a></b> is now live on Storyteller's Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making sure I'm parsing the bit in Summoner about Actions correctly with the replacement of Hyper-Competence with Omnicompetence:<br /> <br /> Does &quot;treating half of the appropriate dicepool as coming from its Skill&quot; mean that a typical homunculus effectively has Attribute 3 + Skill 3 within its areas of expertise and Attribute 1 + Skill 1 for everything else and therefore does not benefit from Omnicompetence's first dot and Jack of All effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T14:50:00-08:00","id":1545886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1535691-shallow-graves-a-player-s-guide-to-deviant-the-renegades?p=1545872#post1545872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making sure I'm parsing the bit in Summoner about Actions correctly with the replacement of Hyper-Competence with Omnicompetence:<br /> <br /> Does &quot;treating half of the appropriate dicepool as coming from its Skill&quot; mean that a typical homunculus effectively has Attribute 3 + Skill 3 within its areas of expertise and Attribute 1 + Skill 1 for everything else and therefore does not benefit from Omnicompetence's first dot and Jack of All effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=